1
00:00:14,980 --> 00:00:24,980
<font color="#0080ff">{\an8}Downloaded From MoviesMod.org</font>

2
00:00:25,980 --> 00:00:27,355
ROSS: <i>Yes?</i>

3
00:00:28,438 --> 00:00:30,063
I'll be right there. Don't move.

4
00:00:45,980 --> 00:00:50,105
PRESCOD: <i>Imagine a world
where information can't be trusted.</i>

5
00:00:52,230 --> 00:00:53,938
<i>Not very hard, is it?</i>

6
00:00:55,563 --> 00:00:57,022
<i>News service says one thing,</i>

7
00:00:58,188 --> 00:00:59,480
<i>website says another.</i>

8
00:01:00,813 --> 00:01:01,813
(VEHICLE PASSING)

9
00:01:01,897 --> 00:01:04,272
<i>Society starts to fray.</i>

10
00:01:05,897 --> 00:01:09,022
<i>All we can turn to
are the people we care about.</i>

11
00:01:10,438 --> 00:01:13,480
<i>But what if those people
weren't who we thought they were?</i>

12
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:18,480
<i>What if the ones closest to us,</i>

13
00:01:19,688 --> 00:01:21,647
<i>the ones we've trusted our whole lives...</i>

14
00:01:21,730 --> 00:01:24,188
(BUZZER SOUNDS)

15
00:01:24,272 --> 00:01:25,647
<i>were someone else entirely?</i>

16
00:01:29,647 --> 00:01:31,980
<i>What if they weren't even human?</i>

17
00:01:38,730 --> 00:01:41,647
Agent Prescod, respectfully...

18
00:01:41,730 --> 00:01:43,022
(INHALES SHARPLY)

19
00:01:43,105 --> 00:01:45,272
uh, what exactly are you talking about?

20
00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:47,147
Chaos.

21
00:01:48,647 --> 00:01:50,147
And that's only the beginning.

22
00:01:50,688 --> 00:01:54,188
Five global terrorist strikes
within the past year.

23
00:01:54,272 --> 00:01:56,522
Each one claimed by a different group.

24
00:01:56,605 --> 00:01:58,230
It's business as usual.

25
00:01:58,313 --> 00:02:01,313
That's precisely
what they want you to think.

26
00:02:01,397 --> 00:02:06,272
Argentina attacks Colombia,
Colombia attacks the Philippines.

27
00:02:06,355 --> 00:02:09,605
A violent chain reaction
consuming the globe.

28
00:02:09,688 --> 00:02:11,772
Do you realize
that the entire world is at war?

29
00:02:11,855 --> 00:02:14,272
Well, the atmosphere has been tense.

30
00:02:14,355 --> 00:02:17,272
There is an architect to that tension,
Agent Ross.

31
00:02:17,355 --> 00:02:19,313
These attacks are escalating.

32
00:02:19,397 --> 00:02:22,188
If they hit the soil
of the major power... Oh.

33
00:02:22,272 --> 00:02:26,022
So you... You think the same people
are behind all of this?

34
00:02:26,813 --> 00:02:28,022
Not people...

35
00:02:30,313 --> 00:02:31,313
Skrulls.

36
00:02:34,022 --> 00:02:36,438
- (CHUCKLES)
- Come on, Ross, you know the stories.

37
00:02:37,105 --> 00:02:38,730
This didn't start yesterday.

38
00:02:38,813 --> 00:02:41,522
It started 30 years ago
when the Skrulls found Earth.

39
00:02:42,313 --> 00:02:46,230
Carol Danvers and Nick Fury
promised to find them a new planet.

40
00:02:46,313 --> 00:02:48,272
But now... (CHUCKLES)

41
00:02:48,355 --> 00:02:52,147
now they don't want just any planet,
they want ours.

42
00:02:53,147 --> 00:02:54,563
Look, can't you see it?

43
00:02:55,522 --> 00:02:58,397
All these groups, they're the same.

44
00:02:58,480 --> 00:03:01,522
Skrulls could be anybody,
anywhere, at any time.

45
00:03:01,605 --> 00:03:04,980
And there is only a tiny handful
known to live on Earth.

46
00:03:05,063 --> 00:03:07,813
- That's barely enough to...
- To what?

47
00:03:07,897 --> 00:03:10,605
You have no goddamn idea
what you're talking about, Ross!

48
00:03:11,688 --> 00:03:13,980
There could be thousands of them,
tens of thousands!

49
00:03:14,063 --> 00:03:15,605
And you would never know.

50
00:03:18,147 --> 00:03:22,897
Okay, Prescod, let's play a little game
of forest for the trees, shall we?

51
00:03:22,980 --> 00:03:27,397
Yes, Skrulls can shapeshift.
Yes, they're looking for a new home.

52
00:03:27,980 --> 00:03:29,063
But, as you say,

53
00:03:29,855 --> 00:03:33,022
the only Skrull contact
has been through Nick Fury.

54
00:03:33,105 --> 00:03:35,772
That means they're our allies.

55
00:03:35,855 --> 00:03:36,855
Then where is Fury?

56
00:03:36,938 --> 00:03:38,313
He's on S.A.B.E.R.!

57
00:03:38,397 --> 00:03:42,563
God... And if I'm gonna bring him down
for whatever the hell this is,

58
00:03:42,647 --> 00:03:46,313
I need to give him something
more than just theories, I need evidence.

59
00:03:57,480 --> 00:03:58,938
All these other attacks,

60
00:04:00,188 --> 00:04:03,522
they would be nothing compared to this.

61
00:04:04,938 --> 00:04:08,522
This is the one
that sets the world on fire.

62
00:04:27,730 --> 00:04:31,522
I stopped filing reports at the office.
Don't know who I can trust anymore.

63
00:04:31,605 --> 00:04:32,938
Other than you...

64
00:04:33,022 --> 00:04:36,313
Hey, Prescod, look,
I'm here to help. Okay?

65
00:04:36,397 --> 00:04:41,772
So... So let me take this
and I'll give the information to Fury.

66
00:04:41,855 --> 00:04:42,980
Okay?

67
00:04:43,063 --> 00:04:44,480
(CHUCKLES) Yeah.

68
00:04:56,772 --> 00:04:58,355
(GASPING)

69
00:05:02,063 --> 00:05:03,230
(GUN FIRES)

70
00:05:05,897 --> 00:05:08,813
(BREATHING RAGGEDLY)

71
00:05:10,355 --> 00:05:12,105
(PANTING)

72
00:05:22,647 --> 00:05:24,647
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

73
00:05:34,272 --> 00:05:35,938
I need an extract. Fast.

74
00:05:37,772 --> 00:05:38,938
<i>I need an extract.</i>

75
00:05:42,355 --> 00:05:44,938
Academica Metro Station,
six blocks northeast.

76
00:05:53,938 --> 00:05:54,938
(MAN YELLS)

77
00:05:55,147 --> 00:05:56,855
(PEOPLE CHATTERING INDISTINCTLY)

78
00:06:01,355 --> 00:06:02,647
(SHOUTS IN RUSSIAN)

79
00:06:05,313 --> 00:06:06,313
(YELLS IN RUSSIAN)

80
00:06:20,730 --> 00:06:21,730
(YELLS IN RUSSIAN)

81
00:06:50,647 --> 00:06:52,313
(MAN SHOUTS IN RUSSIAN)

82
00:06:54,188 --> 00:06:55,355
(PANTING)

83
00:07:00,022 --> 00:07:01,022
(GRUNTS)

84
00:07:09,605 --> 00:07:10,980
(GROANS)

85
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:13,480
Ross.

86
00:07:15,980 --> 00:07:17,063
Show me your hands.

87
00:07:17,813 --> 00:07:18,813
(SPEAKS RUSSIAN)

88
00:07:21,605 --> 00:07:23,688
- Talos.
- It's me.

89
00:07:24,772 --> 00:07:26,355
What the hell are you doing here?

90
00:07:27,063 --> 00:07:28,522
I'm chasing him.

91
00:07:30,397 --> 00:07:31,397
(CHUCKLES)

92
00:07:38,647 --> 00:07:39,980
He was one of you.

93
00:07:40,063 --> 00:07:41,438
No, he's...

94
00:07:42,605 --> 00:07:44,188
He... He's one of them.

95
00:10:34,230 --> 00:10:36,230
(DOOR CLOSES)

96
00:10:38,022 --> 00:10:40,355
(SPACESHIP WHIRRING)

97
00:11:09,647 --> 00:11:10,897
(GRUNTING)

98
00:11:12,397 --> 00:11:13,397
(EXHALES)

99
00:11:19,772 --> 00:11:20,980
Welcome back to Earth.

100
00:11:33,813 --> 00:11:34,980
{\an8}He's upstairs.

101
00:11:48,563 --> 00:11:49,563
Is that from home?

102
00:11:51,105 --> 00:11:52,397
Santo Millika.

103
00:11:52,480 --> 00:11:54,813
That's a Skrull sky plant.

104
00:11:55,480 --> 00:12:00,438
Soren. She brought the seed with her
wherever she went.

105
00:12:00,522 --> 00:12:05,355
And it's changed since she planted it.
It's adapted to the planet.

106
00:12:05,438 --> 00:12:09,147
Yeah, well,
you always believed that was possible.

107
00:12:09,230 --> 00:12:11,272
I still do.

108
00:12:14,813 --> 00:12:15,813
(FURY SIGHS)

109
00:12:18,563 --> 00:12:20,272
I am so sorry.

110
00:12:21,855 --> 00:12:22,855
Me, too.

111
00:12:24,355 --> 00:12:25,772
Soren loved you.

112
00:12:27,605 --> 00:12:29,022
But she worried, mate,

113
00:12:29,105 --> 00:12:32,813
that it would take something like this
to bring you back to Earth.

114
00:12:32,897 --> 00:12:34,355
And I guess she was right.

115
00:12:38,688 --> 00:12:40,397
(SNIFFLES AND EXHALES)

116
00:12:42,022 --> 00:12:43,397
FURY: Tell me about Gravik.

117
00:12:44,647 --> 00:12:47,147
Let's... Let's just
talk about you first, yeah?

118
00:12:49,063 --> 00:12:54,938
We've been helping you for all these years
to ensure that you kept your promise.

119
00:12:55,605 --> 00:13:00,105
But after The Blip, you were different.

120
00:13:01,813 --> 00:13:03,105
And then you disappeared.

121
00:13:05,147 --> 00:13:07,855
Carol Danvers disappeared.

122
00:13:07,938 --> 00:13:10,063
And so did G'iah.

123
00:13:10,147 --> 00:13:13,147
Hold it. Your daughter?
Disappeared too... Where?

124
00:13:13,230 --> 00:13:14,355
She was young.

125
00:13:15,563 --> 00:13:17,855
Angry that our people
still don't have a home.

126
00:13:18,522 --> 00:13:19,813
Many of them are upset.

127
00:13:20,605 --> 00:13:24,355
I got kicked off the Council,
pushed into exile.

128
00:13:25,397 --> 00:13:26,480
But, Gravik...

129
00:13:27,022 --> 00:13:33,980
Gravik, mate, he took your abandonment
that much harder.

130
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:36,647
Come on.

131
00:13:37,563 --> 00:13:41,147
HILL: Gravik is now the newest member
of the Skrull Council.

132
00:13:41,230 --> 00:13:45,063
He preys on the collective rage
of young, displaced Skrulls.

133
00:13:45,147 --> 00:13:46,397
FURY: Where is his ass?

134
00:13:46,480 --> 00:13:48,063
He's here. He's in Russia.

135
00:13:48,147 --> 00:13:50,105
Skrulls are immune to radioactivity

136
00:13:50,188 --> 00:13:53,022
and Russia has the most abandoned
nuclear plants on Earth.

137
00:13:53,105 --> 00:13:57,397
But here's the thing.
These plants, they're not on the books.

138
00:13:58,230 --> 00:13:59,980
And we don't know where he is.

139
00:14:00,063 --> 00:14:02,188
Well, what else do we know
about his plans?

140
00:14:02,897 --> 00:14:04,480
Well, he's already made them.

141
00:14:05,272 --> 00:14:08,480
This is what Agent Ross's imposter
was trying to cover up.

142
00:14:08,563 --> 00:14:11,688
Schematics for a dirty bomb
intercepted by Prescod.

143
00:14:11,772 --> 00:14:15,313
Prescod had been monitoring
a new radical group called the AAR,

144
00:14:15,397 --> 00:14:16,688
Americans Against Russia,

145
00:14:16,772 --> 00:14:20,438
which he believed to be the next
Skrull front for a terrorist attack.

146
00:14:20,522 --> 00:14:23,980
Gravik's trying to start a war between
Russia and the United States?

147
00:14:24,063 --> 00:14:25,230
That was Prescod's theory.

148
00:14:25,313 --> 00:14:27,230
And he's gonna use this bomb to do it?

149
00:14:27,980 --> 00:14:29,855
Does he have the materials for that?

150
00:14:29,938 --> 00:14:32,230
HILL: A weapons cache in Kazakhstan,

151
00:14:32,313 --> 00:14:34,730
raided the same day
that Prescod was killed.

152
00:14:35,397 --> 00:14:37,397
TALOS: We brought you here for a reason.

153
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:39,397
If he succeeds, um,

154
00:14:40,230 --> 00:14:42,480
your species will cease to exist.

155
00:14:48,147 --> 00:14:49,188
Shit.

156
00:14:50,022 --> 00:14:51,397
I'm going for a walk.

157
00:14:52,022 --> 00:14:54,272
You're going for a walk in Moscow
at night?

158
00:14:54,355 --> 00:14:56,897
(STAMMERS) Well, you're gonna stand out.

159
00:14:59,438 --> 00:15:00,605
(DOOR CLOSES)

160
00:15:02,813 --> 00:15:04,605
RHODEY: We have a situation,
Mr. President.

161
00:15:04,688 --> 00:15:06,522
RITSON: Concerning?
RHODEY: Agent Fury.

162
00:15:06,605 --> 00:15:08,565
We've just received word
that he's left S.A.B.E.R.

163
00:15:08,605 --> 00:15:10,355
What do you mean, "He left S.A.B.E.R.?"

164
00:15:10,938 --> 00:15:14,313
Well, I can try to think of
a different word. Abandoned, departed...

165
00:15:14,397 --> 00:15:17,605
Agent Fury is building up the most
complex aerospace defense system

166
00:15:17,688 --> 00:15:19,313
in the history of mankind.

167
00:15:19,397 --> 00:15:21,355
- He can't just leave.
- No, I agree, sir.

168
00:15:21,438 --> 00:15:22,563
And unfortunately,

169
00:15:22,647 --> 00:15:26,272
we also intercepted an encrypted message
from Agent Hill to Agent Fury.

170
00:15:26,355 --> 00:15:30,147
We haven't been able to decode it yet,
but we know they're old friends.

171
00:15:30,230 --> 00:15:34,147
Given the fact that I could reach
neither Agent Hill nor Agent Fury,

172
00:15:35,522 --> 00:15:36,980
they're effectively AWOL.

173
00:15:37,772 --> 00:15:38,855
Deal with it.

174
00:15:38,938 --> 00:15:40,022
RHODEY: Yes, sir.

175
00:15:50,730 --> 00:15:51,730
(SPEAKS INDISTINCTLY)

176
00:15:55,938 --> 00:15:57,688
(WOMAN SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

177
00:16:26,980 --> 00:16:29,188
(SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

178
00:16:37,980 --> 00:16:39,230
(FURY GROANS)

179
00:16:50,480 --> 00:16:52,105
WOMAN: (IN ENGLISH)This is so exciting.

180
00:16:52,188 --> 00:16:54,397
Let's see, large Black man, Moscow.

181
00:16:54,480 --> 00:16:58,688
Well, it could either be Nick Fury,
or the ghost of Paul Robeson.

182
00:16:58,772 --> 00:17:00,480
Okay, go ahead, take the hood off.

183
00:17:01,147 --> 00:17:04,813
Oh! Damn, and I was hoping for a command
performance of <i>Ol' Man River.</i>

184
00:17:04,897 --> 00:17:07,355
Good to see you too, Sonya.

185
00:17:07,438 --> 00:17:13,522
So, did you just have me extraordinarily
renditioned by a group of your thugs?

186
00:17:13,605 --> 00:17:15,022
Were you lot extraordinary?

187
00:17:15,688 --> 00:17:16,688
Oh!

188
00:17:16,772 --> 00:17:19,272
You usually only
scratch the surface of mediocrity.

189
00:17:19,355 --> 00:17:22,272
You must be finally
putting it all together. Well done.

190
00:17:22,355 --> 00:17:24,313
Okay. You can go. That's... That'll do.

191
00:17:26,022 --> 00:17:28,397
"Extraordinary," well, that's wonderful.

192
00:17:30,522 --> 00:17:32,897
It is so good to see you.

193
00:17:34,730 --> 00:17:37,772
You look amazing.

194
00:17:37,855 --> 00:17:38,980
Thanks.

195
00:17:40,272 --> 00:17:42,397
- Drink?
- FURY: Love one.

196
00:17:43,355 --> 00:17:46,730
Do you have some sort of clock fetish
that you've been

197
00:17:46,813 --> 00:17:49,272
- keeping from me all these years?
- (WHIRRING)

198
00:17:49,355 --> 00:17:52,522
SONYA: It was an old English spymaster
that started the tradition.

199
00:17:52,605 --> 00:17:55,313
A clock goes up
when your time in circus is done.

200
00:17:56,147 --> 00:17:59,188
And I like to think I still have
a few juggling acts left in me.

201
00:18:02,938 --> 00:18:05,063
Oh. Make yourself at home, Fury.

202
00:18:08,272 --> 00:18:09,897
- (JAZZ MUSIC PLAYING)
- (SPEAKS RUSSIAN)

203
00:18:09,980 --> 00:18:13,772
(IN ENGLISH) I'm pretty sure you recollect
my drink of choice as bourbon.

204
00:18:13,855 --> 00:18:15,397
I might have welcomed you home,

205
00:18:15,480 --> 00:18:18,272
but I still haven't forgiven you
for destroying my expensive flat.

206
00:18:18,355 --> 00:18:19,480
You mean city.

207
00:18:19,563 --> 00:18:21,355
It's bottom shelf piss for you or nothing.

208
00:18:21,438 --> 00:18:22,563
(SPEAKS RUSSIAN)

209
00:18:25,605 --> 00:18:27,480
(IN ENGLISH)
So, what are you doing in Moscow?

210
00:18:28,105 --> 00:18:32,147
Same as you, trying to kill
the Skrull rebellion in its crib.

211
00:18:32,230 --> 00:18:34,980
You know the rebel leader personally,
don't you?

212
00:18:36,605 --> 00:18:38,063
I knew him.

213
00:18:38,147 --> 00:18:40,730
Is that why you came down
from your space station?

214
00:18:41,313 --> 00:18:42,605
You feel responsible?

215
00:18:47,897 --> 00:18:50,813
What do you know about a heist

216
00:18:50,897 --> 00:18:54,522
at a black market storage facility
in Kazakhstan?

217
00:18:54,605 --> 00:18:56,938
It happened couple days ago.

218
00:18:58,105 --> 00:18:59,272
Doesn't ring a bell.

219
00:19:01,855 --> 00:19:05,813
You know, I may not know
when a Skrull is pretending to be a human,

220
00:19:06,397 --> 00:19:09,313
but I sure as hell know
when a human is lying.

221
00:19:09,397 --> 00:19:12,147
You know damn well
what was in that storage vault.

222
00:19:12,230 --> 00:19:14,022
The fact that you don't know

223
00:19:14,105 --> 00:19:17,313
tells me all I need to know
about this new, rather old Nick Fury.

224
00:19:18,438 --> 00:19:20,730
I think that Thanos's snap changed you.

225
00:19:20,813 --> 00:19:23,563
Taught you that no matter
how hard you fight for what's right,

226
00:19:23,647 --> 00:19:26,188
there's always someone stronger
to undermine you.

227
00:19:27,355 --> 00:19:30,188
You seem to forget this "old Nick Fury"

228
00:19:30,272 --> 00:19:33,480
has 30 years
of hands-on experience with the Skrulls.

229
00:19:34,480 --> 00:19:37,772
I know the nature of this threat
way better than you ever will.

230
00:19:38,730 --> 00:19:42,063
Is that your idea of an offer
of some sort of collaboration between us?

231
00:19:42,147 --> 00:19:44,605
We used to work pretty well together
back in the day.

232
00:19:44,688 --> 00:19:47,313
Back then, you would've seen
my rather mediocre bag men

233
00:19:47,397 --> 00:19:48,522
coming a mile away.

234
00:19:49,188 --> 00:19:50,563
The fact that you didn't see them

235
00:19:50,647 --> 00:19:54,105
means you haven't a hope in hell
of seeing Gravik and his rebels coming.

236
00:19:54,188 --> 00:19:56,772
Which makes you as a partner
rather pointless.

237
00:19:56,855 --> 00:20:00,188
I let your men take me
so I could get to you.

238
00:20:00,772 --> 00:20:04,438
I mean this as a friend, Fury,
but go back to your space station.

239
00:20:05,105 --> 00:20:07,813
You're in no shape
for this fight that lies before us.

240
00:20:08,855 --> 00:20:11,355
I'll have one of my thugs
drop you back at the safe house.

241
00:20:11,438 --> 00:20:13,897
That's all right, I'll walk.

242
00:20:14,688 --> 00:20:16,272
(EXHALES)

243
00:20:16,355 --> 00:20:20,980
If your memory jogs about
that Kazakhstan thing,

244
00:20:22,063 --> 00:20:23,147
call a brother.

245
00:20:29,230 --> 00:20:30,813
(WHIRRING)

246
00:20:43,813 --> 00:20:44,897
GUARD: What do you want?

247
00:20:46,397 --> 00:20:47,813
Home in my own skin.

248
00:21:00,563 --> 00:21:01,813
(DOOR OPENS AND CLOSES)

249
00:21:13,063 --> 00:21:14,438
Take your natural form.

250
00:21:38,438 --> 00:21:39,938
Welcome to New Skrullos.

251
00:21:58,313 --> 00:21:59,313
What's your name?

252
00:22:02,063 --> 00:22:03,063
Beto.

253
00:22:04,355 --> 00:22:06,522
When's the last time you ate, Beto?

254
00:22:08,688 --> 00:22:09,938
I don't know.

255
00:22:18,480 --> 00:22:20,063
- This can't be.
- (CHUCKLES)

256
00:22:21,855 --> 00:22:23,980
We grow only Skrull produce here.

257
00:22:25,063 --> 00:22:27,980
Drink Skrull wine, wear Skrull skins.

258
00:22:28,063 --> 00:22:32,480
Whatever dangers you risked getting here,
know, they're worth it.

259
00:22:42,272 --> 00:22:43,438
BETO: Thank you.

260
00:22:44,438 --> 00:22:45,605
You're very welcome.

261
00:23:10,230 --> 00:23:12,230
(CHATTERING INDISTINCTLY)

262
00:23:19,063 --> 00:23:20,063
(MAN SPEAKS INDISTINCTLY)

263
00:23:20,397 --> 00:23:22,605
(CHILDREN LAUGHING AND CHATTERING)

264
00:23:34,022 --> 00:23:35,855
(CHATTERING INDISTINCTLY)

265
00:23:38,897 --> 00:23:40,563
We're over 500 strong now.

266
00:23:41,147 --> 00:23:43,022
BETO: So, is everyone a part of...

267
00:23:43,105 --> 00:23:45,813
The resistance? No.
Gravik provides refuge.

268
00:23:46,397 --> 00:23:49,730
But if you do choose to be a warrior,
there is one advantage.

269
00:23:49,813 --> 00:23:51,355
Oh, yeah? What's that?

270
00:23:51,438 --> 00:23:52,605
You get to leave.

271
00:23:53,230 --> 00:23:55,063
Everyone else stays in the compound.

272
00:23:55,980 --> 00:23:59,647
The warriors keep our human form,
the longer we're attached to our shells,

273
00:23:59,730 --> 00:24:03,397
the less likely we can be identified
by humans and Skrulls alike.

274
00:24:07,480 --> 00:24:10,105
Wait here
and someone will get you a proper room.

275
00:24:10,188 --> 00:24:12,897
Prove your loyalty
and Gravik will reward you.

276
00:24:14,688 --> 00:24:15,855
What's behind there?

277
00:24:17,730 --> 00:24:18,730
Victory.

278
00:24:32,980 --> 00:24:35,313
(MAN GRUNTING IN DISTANCE)

279
00:24:45,772 --> 00:24:47,230
What is your name?

280
00:24:47,313 --> 00:24:48,605
BROGAN: Warrior.

281
00:24:48,688 --> 00:24:50,105
What is your fight?

282
00:24:50,188 --> 00:24:51,230
BROGAN: Skrullos.

283
00:24:51,313 --> 00:24:52,605
PAGON: What is your dream?

284
00:24:52,688 --> 00:24:54,772
BROGAN: Home in my own skin.

285
00:24:58,022 --> 00:24:59,647
Bring him his shell.

286
00:24:59,730 --> 00:25:01,480
MAN: (GRUNTS) No. No!

287
00:25:08,980 --> 00:25:13,022
Americans Against Russia,
your dreams are about to come true.

288
00:25:13,605 --> 00:25:14,813
Take his face.

289
00:25:20,397 --> 00:25:21,980
(GROANS)

290
00:25:22,855 --> 00:25:23,855
MAN: No!

291
00:25:29,772 --> 00:25:31,230
(ELECTRICITY CRACKLING)

292
00:25:32,772 --> 00:25:34,105
Now take his mind.

293
00:25:52,355 --> 00:25:55,397
SONYA: Skrulls have infiltrated
the ranks of major world powers.

294
00:25:55,480 --> 00:25:56,980
MAN: <i>Where is the proof?</i>

295
00:25:57,063 --> 00:25:58,980
<i>How about the arrival of Agent Fury?</i>

296
00:25:59,063 --> 00:26:02,397
<i>For a man who sworn off Earth,
he would not have returned without cause.</i>

297
00:26:02,480 --> 00:26:03,772
You got that right.

298
00:26:03,855 --> 00:26:06,938
<i>Gravik has something very big
up his sleeve.</i>

299
00:26:07,022 --> 00:26:09,647
<i>But the immediate threat
remains the bombs.</i>

300
00:26:09,730 --> 00:26:13,355
<i>Five specialists in Moscow
are capable of building such an explosive.</i>

301
00:26:13,438 --> 00:26:14,897
<i>My money's on this one.</i>

302
00:26:15,563 --> 00:26:18,022
<i>Vasily Poprishchin.
Former Chechnyan rebel,</i>

303
00:26:18,105 --> 00:26:20,105
<i>owns a high-end gallery
in the city center,</i>

304
00:26:20,188 --> 00:26:23,563
<i>restores pigmented paintings
and radioactivated bombs.</i>

305
00:26:23,647 --> 00:26:25,355
MAN: <i>Send in a raid now.</i>

306
00:26:25,438 --> 00:26:26,730
SONYA: <i>If by "now" you mean,</i>

307
00:26:26,813 --> 00:26:29,230
<i>"Wait until a Skrull rebel
picks up a device</i>

308
00:26:29,313 --> 00:26:32,730
<i>in order to follow them to their hideout,"
then, yes, I totally agree.</i>

309
00:26:33,813 --> 00:26:34,938
She's cheeky.

310
00:26:35,022 --> 00:26:37,397
Yeah, 'till she sees
an ugly-ass Skrull like you.

311
00:26:37,480 --> 00:26:38,980
Then she goes into hunting mode.

312
00:26:39,063 --> 00:26:41,855
I'm considered good-looking
amongst my kind.

313
00:26:41,938 --> 00:26:44,605
I know a bunch of good-looking Skrull.
And you ain't one of them.

314
00:26:44,688 --> 00:26:46,605
HILL: All right, guys,
what is the play here?

315
00:26:46,688 --> 00:26:49,188
I say we visit this Rusky bomb builder.

316
00:26:49,272 --> 00:26:51,022
Sonya will already have agents there.

317
00:26:51,105 --> 00:26:52,813
Who we will incapacitate.

318
00:26:52,897 --> 00:26:54,022
TALOS: Hold on, stop.

319
00:26:54,105 --> 00:26:58,355
You're talking about
attacking MI6 operatives?

320
00:26:58,438 --> 00:27:00,397
FURY: Talos,
let me explain something to you.

321
00:27:00,480 --> 00:27:03,105
We're no longer
in "just a war" with Gravik.

322
00:27:03,188 --> 00:27:07,647
We are in a race with Sonya Falsworth,
who celebrates a scorched-Earth policy,

323
00:27:07,730 --> 00:27:10,105
meaning, she will annihilate
any and everyone

324
00:27:10,188 --> 00:27:12,605
who's ever even heard the name "Gravik."

325
00:27:13,063 --> 00:27:15,772
You wanna save innocent Skrulls,
you'll have to hurt some people.

326
00:27:15,855 --> 00:27:16,855
All right...

327
00:27:16,938 --> 00:27:18,647
FURY: Look, Gravik knows that...

328
00:27:19,480 --> 00:27:20,605
mercy's your weakness.

329
00:27:21,272 --> 00:27:22,897
Time for you to prove him wrong.

330
00:27:23,980 --> 00:27:24,980
Hmm?

331
00:27:25,897 --> 00:27:26,897
Yeah, okay.

332
00:27:49,063 --> 00:27:50,355
PAGON: Fury's in town, G.

333
00:27:52,813 --> 00:27:53,855
Is he?

334
00:27:54,813 --> 00:27:57,022
Our man says it's nothing to worry about.

335
00:27:57,105 --> 00:28:00,480
He's washed up, walks with a limp,
can barely see with the good eye.

336
00:28:01,355 --> 00:28:03,813
I see you've kept the circle tight
on this one.

337
00:28:05,022 --> 00:28:07,063
We're the circle. No one else.

338
00:28:07,730 --> 00:28:09,480
Is that to protect me, or the cause?

339
00:28:15,147 --> 00:28:17,897
You are the cause.

340
00:28:17,980 --> 00:28:19,188
I'm not the cause.

341
00:28:20,688 --> 00:28:22,105
Cause is home.

342
00:28:22,772 --> 00:28:23,772
Yes, sir.

343
00:28:24,897 --> 00:28:28,522
GRAVIK: We go tomorrow
and we don't stop until Earth is ours.

344
00:28:33,147 --> 00:28:35,313
G'IAH: What about it?
BETO: This place is massive.

345
00:28:35,397 --> 00:28:36,397
PAGON: You.

346
00:28:37,063 --> 00:28:38,063
Come with me.

347
00:28:46,063 --> 00:28:47,272
Zirksu will drive you.

348
00:28:47,938 --> 00:28:49,772
You take the cash to this address.

349
00:28:49,855 --> 00:28:52,022
You deal with Poprishchin and no one else.

350
00:28:52,105 --> 00:28:53,438
He'll give you two bags.

351
00:28:53,522 --> 00:28:56,480
You get 'em to the Moscow safe house
undisturbed and intact.

352
00:29:10,688 --> 00:29:11,938
(ENGINE STARTS)

353
00:29:39,688 --> 00:29:41,063
Where's the bloody coffee?

354
00:29:46,688 --> 00:29:48,188
FURY: What's our MI6 status?

355
00:29:54,188 --> 00:29:55,188
All set.

356
00:30:09,022 --> 00:30:10,397
You Poprishchin?

357
00:30:11,230 --> 00:30:12,230
(SPEAKS RUSSIAN)

358
00:30:17,272 --> 00:30:19,647
FURY: Oh, shit.
TALOS: I got it, mate.

359
00:30:23,188 --> 00:30:25,605
Not bad for a 136-year-old.

360
00:30:25,688 --> 00:30:29,147
Well, you know,
I'm not even 40 in human years.

361
00:30:29,230 --> 00:30:32,438
I haven't even gone
on my midlife crisis shopping spree yet.

362
00:30:33,188 --> 00:30:34,188
Hey.

363
00:30:34,897 --> 00:30:36,522
What'd you get for yours?

364
00:30:38,063 --> 00:30:39,063
The Avengers.

365
00:30:54,855 --> 00:30:55,855
{\an8}(SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

366
00:30:58,480 --> 00:31:01,563
(IN ENGLISH) No, mate, we don't want
any of your shitty paintings.

367
00:31:02,313 --> 00:31:03,855
Then exactly what do you want?

368
00:31:04,855 --> 00:31:06,272
Some damn good answers.

369
00:31:08,647 --> 00:31:10,188
(INAUDIBLE)

370
00:31:18,355 --> 00:31:20,688
I've got eyes
on a possible person of interest.

371
00:31:20,772 --> 00:31:22,730
Initiating foot pursuit.
I'll keep you posted.

372
00:31:22,813 --> 00:31:24,105
Yeah, just keep me informed.

373
00:31:24,688 --> 00:31:27,730
I'm sorry, but you gentlemen
will have to call at another time.

374
00:31:27,813 --> 00:31:30,522
- I'm late for an appointment.
- Oh! Oh, who you meetin' with?

375
00:31:30,605 --> 00:31:32,147
My wife, Mister...

376
00:31:32,313 --> 00:31:33,313
Oh!

377
00:31:33,563 --> 00:31:35,230
Ooh! Damn, this is nice.

378
00:31:35,313 --> 00:31:38,272
That chair belonged to Louis XV.
It's priceless.

379
00:31:38,355 --> 00:31:42,397
Everything is priceless till it gets
blown to bits in a hail of bullets.

380
00:31:42,480 --> 00:31:43,480
(SIGHS)

381
00:31:43,563 --> 00:31:47,522
Agent Keller, anything in our file
about this one having a wife?

382
00:31:47,605 --> 00:31:49,438
Yeah, has an ex-wife,

383
00:31:49,522 --> 00:31:51,647
lives in Miami with a soccer player.

384
00:31:52,438 --> 00:31:56,563
Oh, so we gonna go ahead
and call that a lie.

385
00:31:56,647 --> 00:31:58,480
Everybody gets one.

386
00:31:58,563 --> 00:32:00,772
Nobody gets two.

387
00:32:01,772 --> 00:32:04,188
So, last chance.

388
00:32:04,647 --> 00:32:06,730
Who are you going to meet?

389
00:32:08,480 --> 00:32:11,272
Perhaps we'd all be more comfortable
in the gallery space

390
00:32:11,355 --> 00:32:12,897
where there is more natural light.

391
00:32:12,980 --> 00:32:16,355
You got any more of these comfortable-ass
Louis XIV chairs in there?

392
00:32:16,438 --> 00:32:17,522
Mmm-mmm.

393
00:32:17,605 --> 00:32:18,897
How about a dirty bomb?

394
00:32:19,480 --> 00:32:22,063
Or you keep that in a crate
in here somewhere?

395
00:32:22,772 --> 00:32:25,938
I'm sorry, I do not know this term.
Dirty bomb?

396
00:32:26,022 --> 00:32:29,022
Boom, goes the dynamite! Lie number two.

397
00:32:29,480 --> 00:32:34,688
I just told you.
Everybody gets one, nobody gets two.

398
00:32:35,522 --> 00:32:36,813
You going to shoot me?

399
00:32:36,897 --> 00:32:39,480
Maybe. Well, probably.

400
00:32:40,105 --> 00:32:41,772
- (GROANS)
- But not right now.

401
00:32:43,022 --> 00:32:44,230
Where are the bombs?

402
00:32:47,313 --> 00:32:48,772
Your name's not Keller.

403
00:32:52,813 --> 00:32:53,938
(CHUCKLES)

404
00:32:54,022 --> 00:32:55,022
Skrull.

405
00:32:55,105 --> 00:32:56,355
Your name is Talos.

406
00:32:58,522 --> 00:32:59,938
(GRUNTS)

407
00:33:00,022 --> 00:33:01,147
Talos?

408
00:33:02,230 --> 00:33:03,313
I got this.

409
00:33:03,397 --> 00:33:04,480
You sure?

410
00:33:10,772 --> 00:33:12,147
TALOS: This is my fight!

411
00:33:12,230 --> 00:33:13,897
I said no!

412
00:33:15,355 --> 00:33:16,397
(GROANS)

413
00:33:26,522 --> 00:33:28,063
(POPRISHCHIN CHOKING)

414
00:33:28,147 --> 00:33:29,980
Tell me where the bombs are!

415
00:33:30,063 --> 00:33:31,897
You betray your own people.

416
00:33:35,938 --> 00:33:38,105
(GUN FIRING)

417
00:33:50,980 --> 00:33:51,980
Come on.

418
00:33:55,522 --> 00:33:56,772
I said no.

419
00:33:59,730 --> 00:34:01,022
(SQUELCHING)

420
00:35:01,730 --> 00:35:02,897
(TRAIN HORN BLOWS)

421
00:35:03,480 --> 00:35:05,397
(TRAIN PASSING)

422
00:35:05,480 --> 00:35:07,480
(BOTH GRUNTING)

423
00:35:17,105 --> 00:35:18,313
(GROANS)

424
00:35:20,480 --> 00:35:21,522
Where'd he go?

425
00:35:21,605 --> 00:35:22,772
She.

426
00:35:24,397 --> 00:35:29,438
Stop! Stop! Stop!

427
00:35:31,188 --> 00:35:32,605
Last warning!

428
00:35:39,230 --> 00:35:41,563
It's what you always say
but there's always another.

429
00:35:44,313 --> 00:35:45,438
G'iah.

430
00:35:52,188 --> 00:35:54,063
- Give me the bombs.
- No.

431
00:35:55,105 --> 00:35:58,188
I know you're angry. This isn't you.

432
00:35:58,272 --> 00:36:00,730
This is not
what your mother would've wanted.

433
00:36:00,813 --> 00:36:02,730
Mum doesn't know what she wants.

434
00:36:03,813 --> 00:36:07,480
Her last words, "Find G'iah."

435
00:36:10,105 --> 00:36:11,313
What?

436
00:36:13,897 --> 00:36:14,938
She's dead.

437
00:36:21,438 --> 00:36:22,522
How?

438
00:36:24,730 --> 00:36:28,480
Why don't you ask
the people that you work for?

439
00:36:32,272 --> 00:36:35,313
Why don't you
just give me the bomb, please?

440
00:36:37,188 --> 00:36:40,647
G'iah, give me the bomb.

441
00:36:42,647 --> 00:36:45,022
- I can't.
- Just hand it over.

442
00:36:45,105 --> 00:36:46,230
And you'll walk away.

443
00:36:47,272 --> 00:36:50,355
'Cause you know that I'll protect you.

444
00:36:50,438 --> 00:36:54,022
- You can't protect anyone.
- G'iah, I know...

445
00:37:26,063 --> 00:37:28,147
(SOBBING)

446
00:37:38,897 --> 00:37:40,897
(PEOPLE CHATTERING INDISTINCTLY)

447
00:37:49,355 --> 00:37:50,480
{\an8}(SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

448
00:37:57,355 --> 00:37:58,355
{\an8}(DRUNK MAN SPEAKING)

449
00:38:38,397 --> 00:38:40,039
(IN ENGLISH) Making friends
with the locals?

450
00:38:40,063 --> 00:38:41,272
(FURY CHUCKLES)

451
00:38:41,355 --> 00:38:47,313
How do you think
we kept the Cold War from going hot?

452
00:38:48,688 --> 00:38:50,480
Spooks like me buying shots.

453
00:38:50,563 --> 00:38:51,938
You can't say that.

454
00:38:52,022 --> 00:38:54,188
No. You can't say that.

455
00:38:57,355 --> 00:38:58,355
Mmm!

456
00:38:59,355 --> 00:39:00,397
(HILL EXHALES)

457
00:39:01,730 --> 00:39:03,438
It's good to have you back, Fury.

458
00:39:03,897 --> 00:39:08,272
Is that sincere
or you just covering your bases?

459
00:39:08,355 --> 00:39:10,063
You'll tell me why you abandoned Earth?

460
00:39:10,147 --> 00:39:12,480
Well, building out S.A.B.E.R.

461
00:39:12,563 --> 00:39:15,647
Traditionally, we tell the truth
during our chess games.

462
00:39:15,730 --> 00:39:18,980
Maybe that has changed too, though,
I don't know.

463
00:39:19,855 --> 00:39:24,313
Okay, let's just say
I had a crisis of faith.

464
00:39:25,063 --> 00:39:26,730
So why'd you come back?

465
00:39:28,105 --> 00:39:29,438
It followed me up there,

466
00:39:30,438 --> 00:39:33,355
and I owe it to Talos.

467
00:39:33,438 --> 00:39:35,772
You sure you're not talking
about someone else?

468
00:39:42,313 --> 00:39:43,313
You gonna move?

469
00:39:45,480 --> 00:39:46,563
I haven't decided.

470
00:39:48,105 --> 00:39:49,855
See, that's what I'm worried about.

471
00:39:50,605 --> 00:39:52,813
The Fury I knew
was always three steps ahead.

472
00:39:54,938 --> 00:39:58,522
If I remember correctly, you called me.

473
00:39:59,022 --> 00:40:00,688
Upon Talos's request.

474
00:40:01,855 --> 00:40:05,480
Your lack of contact over the past
few years sent a pretty clear message.

475
00:40:05,563 --> 00:40:06,813
Meaning?

476
00:40:13,522 --> 00:40:15,563
You're not ready for this, Fury.

477
00:40:17,105 --> 00:40:18,980
There's a very real threat out there.

478
00:40:19,063 --> 00:40:22,355
You were never the same after The Blip.

479
00:40:22,438 --> 00:40:25,438
You always told me there is no shame

480
00:40:25,522 --> 00:40:28,730
in walking away
when the steps are uncertain.

481
00:40:30,522 --> 00:40:31,730
So check your footing.

482
00:40:33,147 --> 00:40:34,772
Otherwise someone's gonna get hurt.

483
00:40:48,688 --> 00:40:49,855
Oh, no.

484
00:40:51,147 --> 00:40:52,272
Mother...

485
00:41:26,022 --> 00:41:27,022
Good work.

486
00:41:27,855 --> 00:41:30,147
I barely made it out.
Someone was waiting for me.

487
00:41:32,938 --> 00:41:34,688
Someone you can identify?

488
00:41:34,772 --> 00:41:35,855
G'IAH: No.

489
00:41:37,647 --> 00:41:39,105
Maybe we postpone the strike.

490
00:41:40,688 --> 00:41:45,480
To the contrary.
Thanks to you, we have the bait.

491
00:42:00,605 --> 00:42:02,605
(SIRENS BLARING IN DISTANCE)

492
00:42:14,063 --> 00:42:15,730
(SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

493
00:42:57,105 --> 00:42:58,355
Thanks for coming to see me.

494
00:42:58,438 --> 00:43:01,438
You don't see me because I'm not here.

495
00:43:02,188 --> 00:43:03,980
I understand. You're taking a risk.

496
00:43:04,355 --> 00:43:05,480
A risk?

497
00:43:06,147 --> 00:43:10,147
Is that what you explained to Mum,
that following you could get her killed?

498
00:43:10,230 --> 00:43:15,480
Your mother died
while you were working for her killer.

499
00:43:16,147 --> 00:43:19,313
So do not take me down that road, G'iah.

500
00:43:19,397 --> 00:43:22,688
You have one chance to save yourself.

501
00:43:22,772 --> 00:43:24,355
And I think you know that.

502
00:43:25,397 --> 00:43:27,105
I think that's why you're here.

503
00:43:35,480 --> 00:43:37,730
The attack is planned for tomorrow.

504
00:43:37,813 --> 00:43:38,938
Unity Day.

505
00:43:40,563 --> 00:43:44,063
There are three bombs.
And Gravik knows you'll be there.

506
00:43:44,813 --> 00:43:46,605
- How?
- I don't know.

507
00:43:47,230 --> 00:43:50,855
There are so many operatives in the field.
A hundred, at least.

508
00:43:51,647 --> 00:43:52,772
Fracking pods?

509
00:43:53,188 --> 00:43:55,813
Most of their identities are kept secret,
even from us.

510
00:44:01,105 --> 00:44:05,980
Your mum would be very proud of you,
you know, for coming to see me.

511
00:44:12,438 --> 00:44:16,522
Tomorrow, there are three couriers,
including me.

512
00:44:16,605 --> 00:44:19,188
All the points
near Vossoyedineniye Square.

513
00:44:20,147 --> 00:44:22,272
I'll mark each bag with infrared spray.

514
00:44:31,688 --> 00:44:33,105
G'iah's come back.

515
00:44:41,313 --> 00:44:43,522
(PEOPLE CHATTERING INDISTINCTLY)

516
00:44:58,438 --> 00:44:59,688
I got eyes on her.

517
00:45:00,897 --> 00:45:02,313
(OVER EARPIECE) <i>Two backpacks.</i>

518
00:45:04,063 --> 00:45:05,105
I got her.

519
00:45:05,188 --> 00:45:07,563
Remember we're tracking the bags,
not the people.

520
00:45:08,230 --> 00:45:10,605
FURY: Lot of backpacks in Central Moscow.

521
00:45:10,688 --> 00:45:13,855
G'iah's painted ours with infrared spray.

522
00:45:14,897 --> 00:45:16,188
Infrared. Got it.

523
00:45:29,188 --> 00:45:30,438
HILL: We missed the pass.

524
00:45:38,730 --> 00:45:40,605
FURY: Got one carrier going northeast.

525
00:45:43,230 --> 00:45:45,688
The other one south. Let's move.

526
00:45:50,813 --> 00:45:52,230
Excuse me. Excuse me!

527
00:45:53,355 --> 00:45:56,147
(THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING)

528
00:46:08,730 --> 00:46:10,813
(PEOPLE CHATTERING INDISTINCTLY)

529
00:46:31,063 --> 00:46:34,855
(OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING)

530
00:46:50,188 --> 00:46:52,480
(THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING)

531
00:47:07,480 --> 00:47:10,230
(OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING)

532
00:47:31,772 --> 00:47:34,438
(OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES)

533
00:47:42,563 --> 00:47:44,605
(THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING)

534
00:48:06,063 --> 00:48:08,563
It's empty. They're decoys.

535
00:48:22,522 --> 00:48:24,188
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

536
00:48:34,438 --> 00:48:36,438
(SCREAMING CONTINUES)

537
00:48:52,980 --> 00:48:54,022
FURY: Hill!

538
00:48:56,230 --> 00:48:58,063
- (GUN FIRES)
- (GROANS)

539
00:49:32,105 --> 00:49:34,938
- Maria!
- It was you.

540
00:49:35,772 --> 00:49:36,772
Not me.

541
00:49:37,563 --> 00:49:38,938
(WHIMPERS)

542
00:49:47,272 --> 00:49:48,647
(FURY GRUNTING)

543
00:52:48,085 --> 00:52:54,607
<font color="#0080ff">{\an8}Downloaded From MoviesMod.org</font>

544
00:52:55,607 --> 00:52:56,648
<i>I'm Nick Fury.</i>

545
00:52:56,732 --> 00:52:58,523
<i>Been riding a desk for the past six years</i>

546
00:52:58,607 --> 00:53:01,047
<i>trying to figure out where
our future enemies are coming from.</i>

547
00:53:01,107 --> 00:53:02,690
Official S.H.I.E.L.D. activity.

548
00:53:02,773 --> 00:53:05,482
Never occurred to me
they would be coming from above.

549
00:53:06,107 --> 00:53:07,107
(GASPS)

550
00:53:07,190 --> 00:53:09,482
You say this thing looked like Coulson?

551
00:53:09,565 --> 00:53:11,107
Mmm. Talked like him, too.

552
00:53:11,607 --> 00:53:12,607
<i>Shapeshifters.</i>

553
00:53:12,690 --> 00:53:14,416
TALOS AS AGENT KELLER:
<i>We can't trust anyone.</i>

554
00:53:14,440 --> 00:53:15,648
<i>Not even our own men.</i>

555
00:53:16,315 --> 00:53:19,023
Now I stand before you
as my true self.

556
00:53:19,898 --> 00:53:21,023
Without deception.

557
00:53:21,107 --> 00:53:22,648
<i>I just wanna talk.</i>

558
00:53:23,565 --> 00:53:26,982
<i>My people lived as refugees, homeless.</i>

559
00:53:27,065 --> 00:53:28,690
- SOREN: Talos!
- Soren.

560
00:53:29,607 --> 00:53:34,065
<i>And the handful of us that are left
will be slaughtered next.</i>

561
00:53:34,148 --> 00:53:37,107
There are thousands of us
separated from each other.

562
00:53:37,190 --> 00:53:39,023
<i>This is just the beginning.</i>

563
00:53:41,232 --> 00:53:42,232
- (GUNSHOT)
- (GROANS)

564
00:53:42,315 --> 00:53:43,315
(SOREN SCREAMS)

565
00:53:45,482 --> 00:53:46,690
They won't be safe here.

566
00:53:47,773 --> 00:53:49,065
<i>They need their own home.</i>

567
00:54:17,732 --> 00:54:19,023
(CHATTERING INDISTINCTLY)

568
00:54:28,440 --> 00:54:30,607
Varra. Welcome.

569
00:54:30,690 --> 00:54:31,773
Thank you, Fury.

570
00:54:32,440 --> 00:54:34,023
I'd like you to meet someone.

571
00:54:35,607 --> 00:54:36,815
This is Gravik.

572
00:54:37,815 --> 00:54:38,815
Gravik.

573
00:54:46,065 --> 00:54:49,398
His parents were killed
in the last stand against the Kree.

574
00:54:49,482 --> 00:54:55,232
He escaped from behind enemy lines,
piloted a ship all on his own.

575
00:54:55,315 --> 00:54:58,398
He is smart, Fury. Knows how to survive.

576
00:54:59,857 --> 00:55:01,482
We could use someone like him.

577
00:55:01,565 --> 00:55:02,732
He's a child.

578
00:55:03,565 --> 00:55:05,023
Only to human eyes.

579
00:55:06,690 --> 00:55:07,982
Just talk to him.

580
00:55:11,148 --> 00:55:12,148
(FURY SIGHS)

581
00:55:17,357 --> 00:55:20,982
Gravik. Sorry to hear about your parents.

582
00:55:22,398 --> 00:55:23,898
They died a brilliant death.

583
00:55:24,690 --> 00:55:25,815
I'm sure they did.

584
00:55:27,648 --> 00:55:28,940
This work here...

585
00:55:30,857 --> 00:55:33,107
you know it's very dangerous.

586
00:55:35,190 --> 00:55:36,440
I'm not afraid.

587
00:55:41,440 --> 00:55:42,773
I can see you're not.

588
00:55:51,857 --> 00:55:56,357
I wanna thank you all for...
For joining me.

589
00:55:57,857 --> 00:56:00,607
I know it's been a...
It's been a rough journey.

590
00:56:02,690 --> 00:56:07,648
We went looking for a home,
found nothing but violence.

591
00:56:08,732 --> 00:56:09,732
And hate.

592
00:56:11,773 --> 00:56:13,523
All of us have lost someone.

593
00:56:15,065 --> 00:56:16,065
Or everyone.

594
00:56:17,523 --> 00:56:23,690
And our entire species
is scattered across the galaxy,

595
00:56:23,773 --> 00:56:28,232
but for those of you
who braved the journey here to Earth,

596
00:56:28,315 --> 00:56:32,273
you did so for one reason.

597
00:56:34,732 --> 00:56:35,898
This man.

598
00:56:38,232 --> 00:56:41,565
This man that I trust.

599
00:56:42,398 --> 00:56:44,482
You know I don't use that word lightly.

600
00:56:47,232 --> 00:56:48,273
Thank you, Talos.

601
00:56:49,482 --> 00:56:50,690
(SIGHS)

602
00:56:50,773 --> 00:56:54,107
My friends, ever since...

603
00:56:55,107 --> 00:56:56,190
Let me rephrase that.

604
00:56:56,273 --> 00:56:59,648
Almost ever since I met Talos,

605
00:57:00,440 --> 00:57:04,607
I believed that humans
and Skrulls can help each other.

606
00:57:07,732 --> 00:57:11,357
The world is facing a serious threat.

607
00:57:11,440 --> 00:57:12,940
And I could use your help.

608
00:57:14,107 --> 00:57:17,982
It would mean putting on a new face

609
00:57:19,273 --> 00:57:20,648
and keeping it.

610
00:57:21,773 --> 00:57:24,732
This is the promise.

611
00:57:25,857 --> 00:57:28,940
While you work to keep my home safe,

612
00:57:29,690 --> 00:57:33,940
Carol Danvers and I
will find you a new one.

613
00:57:36,398 --> 00:57:38,148
Who'll be first to take the pledge?

614
00:57:45,315 --> 00:57:46,315
Thank you, Soren.

615
00:57:50,232 --> 00:57:52,523
You have a courageous mother, G'iah.

616
00:57:56,107 --> 00:57:58,107
(SKRULLS MURMURING INDISTINCTLY)

617
00:58:23,065 --> 00:58:24,607
You keep your word...

618
00:58:26,773 --> 00:58:27,982
I'll keep mine.

619
00:58:33,065 --> 00:58:34,898
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

620
00:58:48,940 --> 00:58:50,607
(WOMAN YELLS INDISTINCTLY)

621
00:58:50,690 --> 00:58:52,690
(PEOPLE CLAMORING)

622
00:59:07,982 --> 00:59:09,398
(MAN YELLING AND SOBBING)

623
00:59:14,857 --> 00:59:15,982
What are you doing?

624
00:59:17,482 --> 00:59:18,732
Let go of me.

625
00:59:18,815 --> 00:59:23,065
I'm an American!
I'm an American! I'm an American!

626
00:59:36,273 --> 00:59:37,315
(GRUNTS)

627
00:59:37,982 --> 00:59:39,065
I'm an American!

628
01:01:54,607 --> 01:01:57,065
(WOMAN SPEAKING IN RUSSIAN
OVER PA)

629
01:02:04,398 --> 01:02:05,565
{\an8}(SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

630
01:02:34,607 --> 01:02:35,607
(SIGHS)

631
01:02:36,440 --> 01:02:37,523
They've gone.

632
01:02:51,898 --> 01:02:52,940
(SIGHS)

633
01:02:54,607 --> 01:02:56,398
You hear anything from G'iah yet?

634
01:02:57,523 --> 01:02:58,940
No, nothing. Not yet.

635
01:03:09,273 --> 01:03:10,398
(CLEARS THROAT)

636
01:03:14,357 --> 01:03:19,482
When me and my mama used to
take these long train rides to Detroit...

637
01:03:20,690 --> 01:03:24,065
You know, train travel back then
wasn't nowhere near this elegant.

638
01:03:25,190 --> 01:03:28,523
Comin' out of Alabama,
we always had to ride in the colored car.

639
01:03:29,690 --> 01:03:34,398
It was hot, sweaty.
Bathroom didn't work half the time.

640
01:03:36,190 --> 01:03:38,773
And we couldn't go in the dining car.

641
01:03:39,815 --> 01:03:46,065
So, we brought fried chicken, white bread,
deviled eggs, and pound cake in a shoebox.

642
01:03:46,148 --> 01:03:47,315
(CHUCKLES)

643
01:03:48,607 --> 01:03:52,982
Mmm. Half hour after the train pulled out,
that chicken be gone!

644
01:03:53,065 --> 01:03:55,190
Smelt way too good to wait.

645
01:03:56,398 --> 01:03:57,815
On these long rides,

646
01:03:57,898 --> 01:04:03,732
me and my mother would make up games,
pass the time.

647
01:04:03,815 --> 01:04:05,732
"Tell Me Somethin' I Don't Know."

648
01:04:05,815 --> 01:04:08,648
That was one of her favorites.

649
01:04:08,732 --> 01:04:15,148
One time she said, "Tell me somethin'
I don't know about you and Suzie."

650
01:04:15,815 --> 01:04:20,440
Me and Suzie had a standing game of doctor
we'd been playin'

651
01:04:20,523 --> 01:04:22,565
behind Old Man Jackson's barn.

652
01:04:22,648 --> 01:04:26,315
Suffice it to say,
I wasn't about to tell her about that.

653
01:04:27,148 --> 01:04:29,898
So, I made up something crazy like,

654
01:04:29,982 --> 01:04:33,232
"Me and Suzie
saw a bullfrog with polka dots."

655
01:04:33,315 --> 01:04:34,315
(LAUGHS)

656
01:04:34,398 --> 01:04:35,857
My mama just smiled.

657
01:04:35,940 --> 01:04:38,732
Even though I'd lied through my teeth,

658
01:04:40,232 --> 01:04:42,273
the mere fact that I did that,

659
01:04:42,357 --> 01:04:47,190
told her everything she needed to know
about me and Suzie.

660
01:04:48,148 --> 01:04:49,190
Mmm.

661
01:04:52,940 --> 01:04:55,023
Well, you wanna go a few rounds?

662
01:04:56,273 --> 01:04:57,315
Sure.

663
01:05:01,357 --> 01:05:05,773
Tell me something I don't know
about the destruction of Skrullos.

664
01:05:07,107 --> 01:05:12,107
You know everything
there is to know about it, Fury.

665
01:05:12,690 --> 01:05:17,940
Name of the game
is Tell Me Something I Don't Know.

666
01:05:21,023 --> 01:05:24,440
We were overpowered by the Kree.
We held 'em off for as long as we could.

667
01:05:24,523 --> 01:05:27,398
When we couldn't hold 'em off any longer,

668
01:05:27,482 --> 01:05:31,482
the million of us that were left, we fled.

669
01:05:32,440 --> 01:05:33,523
FURY: Interesting.

670
01:05:34,482 --> 01:05:40,107
Tell me something I don't know
about the Skrulls that fled.

671
01:05:42,898 --> 01:05:43,940
Um...

672
01:05:45,732 --> 01:05:46,732
They're here.

673
01:05:48,023 --> 01:05:49,065
Who's here?

674
01:05:51,440 --> 01:05:52,773
All of us.

675
01:05:52,857 --> 01:05:53,982
Wait. Whoa, whoa, whoa!

676
01:05:54,065 --> 01:05:59,732
You're tellin' me there's a million
Skrulls walking amongst us right now?

677
01:05:59,815 --> 01:06:03,107
Have you lost your reptilian-ass mind?

678
01:06:03,190 --> 01:06:04,482
I sent out the call

679
01:06:05,232 --> 01:06:10,398
and every Skrull that isn't
in Emperor Drogge's colony, they answered.

680
01:06:11,690 --> 01:06:12,732
You lied to me!

681
01:06:13,523 --> 01:06:16,773
Hey, we were being hunted
across the universe.

682
01:06:16,857 --> 01:06:18,232
I had two choices,

683
01:06:18,315 --> 01:06:22,107
I could let my people be annihilated
or summon 'em here to Earth.

684
01:06:22,190 --> 01:06:24,124
- What would you have done?
- This ain't about me!

685
01:06:24,148 --> 01:06:27,273
Oh, right. But you're fine using us
as your spies and your errand boys,

686
01:06:27,357 --> 01:06:28,523
long as it's on your terms.

687
01:06:28,607 --> 01:06:31,815
The host gets to set the terms
of the visitation.

688
01:06:31,898 --> 01:06:34,565
What happens
when the host disappears, huh?

689
01:06:34,648 --> 01:06:35,815
'Cause you were gone!

690
01:06:35,898 --> 01:06:38,607
And I didn't think you were coming back,
I really didn't.

691
01:06:38,690 --> 01:06:40,523
And even when you did come back,

692
01:06:40,607 --> 01:06:43,023
there was no talking to you
about anything real.

693
01:06:43,107 --> 01:06:45,440
Your boots barely hit Earth.
(SNAPS FINGERS)

694
01:06:46,190 --> 01:06:50,315
And, "Oh, it's too heavy here, man.
I gotta go up to my space station."

695
01:06:50,398 --> 01:06:51,982
You've been up there for years!

696
01:06:52,065 --> 01:06:53,940
You knew how to get
in touch with me, Talos,

697
01:06:54,023 --> 01:06:57,982
and you didn't
because you didn't want me to know.

698
01:06:59,690 --> 01:07:03,190
My hope...
My hope is that with your help...

699
01:07:04,732 --> 01:07:07,315
Skrulls and humans can coexist,
here on Earth.

700
01:07:07,398 --> 01:07:11,357
Human can't coexist with each other!
You've been here long enough to know that!

701
01:07:11,440 --> 01:07:14,940
We've been at war with each other
since we could walk upright!

702
01:07:15,023 --> 01:07:19,607
There is not enough room or tolerance
on this planet for another species!

703
01:07:19,690 --> 01:07:21,690
(WOMAN SPEAKING RUSSIAN OVER PA)

704
01:07:24,065 --> 01:07:26,523
Matter of fact,
neither is this train compartment.

705
01:07:26,607 --> 01:07:27,982
I think this is your stop.

706
01:07:29,898 --> 01:07:31,898
(WOMAN CONTINUES ON PA)

707
01:07:47,482 --> 01:07:48,857
Oh, my God.

708
01:08:15,815 --> 01:08:17,815
(SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING)

709
01:08:51,773 --> 01:08:53,148
Elizabeth.

710
01:08:54,273 --> 01:08:55,273
Were you there?

711
01:08:57,273 --> 01:08:58,273
Yeah.

712
01:09:02,440 --> 01:09:04,107
How did it happen?

713
01:09:06,565 --> 01:09:07,648
It happened quickly.

714
01:09:08,398 --> 01:09:11,607
Don't you be one of those bastards
who gives me a platitude

715
01:09:11,690 --> 01:09:13,315
when I'm looking for the truth!

716
01:09:15,190 --> 01:09:17,690
That one, over there.
You know what he told me?

717
01:09:17,773 --> 01:09:21,148
He told me that
my nation owes me a debt of gratitude.

718
01:09:21,232 --> 01:09:25,315
But he won't even tell me where
on Planet Earth my daughter was killed.

719
01:09:26,107 --> 01:09:29,898
So apparently, facts are not included
in the debt I'm owed.

720
01:09:33,482 --> 01:09:34,898
She died in Moscow.

721
01:09:35,898 --> 01:09:37,940
We were there trying to stop the attack.

722
01:09:39,107 --> 01:09:40,523
Someone set a trap.

723
01:09:41,815 --> 01:09:43,482
- For her?
- No, for me.

724
01:09:44,065 --> 01:09:47,398
Someone wanted to hurt me...

725
01:09:49,190 --> 01:09:50,482
so they hurt her.

726
01:09:52,273 --> 01:09:53,273
Oh.

727
01:09:54,898 --> 01:09:59,857
So, you're the reason I'm taking
my daughter back home in a box.

728
01:10:03,190 --> 01:10:05,607
I'm sorry
I couldn't protect her, Elizabeth.

729
01:10:07,315 --> 01:10:08,732
You're Nick Fury.

730
01:10:10,148 --> 01:10:11,815
Maria believed in you.

731
01:10:12,523 --> 01:10:15,107
She would've followed you
to the gates of hell and back.

732
01:10:17,982 --> 01:10:18,982
(SIGHS)

733
01:10:19,065 --> 01:10:25,190
Look, I don't know
what Maria died for out there.

734
01:10:25,857 --> 01:10:29,898
But whatever it was,
don't let it be for nothing.

735
01:10:39,482 --> 01:10:41,162
NEWSCASTER: <i>Developing Story at this hour.</i>

736
01:10:41,232 --> 01:10:44,815
{\an8}<i>Several bombs exploded today
at an annual celebration in Moscow,</i>

737
01:10:44,898 --> 01:10:47,065
{\an8}<i>killing at least 2,000 civilians.</i>

738
01:10:47,148 --> 01:10:49,190
{\an8}<i>One suspect is currently in custody,</i>

739
01:10:49,273 --> 01:10:52,232
{\an8}<i>identified as a leading member
of the online fringe group,</i>

740
01:10:52,315 --> 01:10:54,065
{\an8}<i>Americans Against Russia.</i>

741
01:10:54,148 --> 01:10:57,398
{\an8}<i>The UK Prime Minister
was quick to denounce the attack,</i>

742
01:10:57,482 --> 01:10:59,523
{\an8}<i>while the NATO Secretary-General says...</i>

743
01:10:59,607 --> 01:11:00,607
{\an8}(READING)

744
01:11:02,940 --> 01:11:07,023
{\an8}<i>Despite the outpouring of condemnation,
all signs point towards</i>

745
01:11:07,107 --> 01:11:08,940
{\an8}<i>imminent retaliation from Russia</i>

746
01:11:09,023 --> 01:11:10,398
{\an8}<i>for what the Kremlin regards</i>

747
01:11:10,482 --> 01:11:14,440
{\an8}<i>as an all-out declaration of war
by the Americans.</i>

748
01:11:14,523 --> 01:11:17,732
{\an8}<i>They're all saying
we had something to do with Moscow.</i>

749
01:11:17,815 --> 01:11:19,148
{\an8}<i>Well, I call bull on that.</i>

750
01:11:19,232 --> 01:11:23,523
{\an8}<i>There's no way that Moscow attack
was committed by Americans.</i>

751
01:11:23,607 --> 01:11:26,315
<i>This has got false flag
written all over it.</i>

752
01:11:40,190 --> 01:11:42,107
How did you know Fury would be there?

753
01:11:43,357 --> 01:11:44,357
I didn't.

754
01:11:45,190 --> 01:11:48,690
Well, not to a certainty. But I hoped.

755
01:11:52,398 --> 01:11:54,565
I wanted to see how much of him was left.

756
01:11:56,523 --> 01:11:57,523
And?

757
01:12:00,857 --> 01:12:04,523
He's just vapors. Old.

758
01:12:06,148 --> 01:12:08,482
You know,
I could've killed him if I wanted to.

759
01:12:10,398 --> 01:12:13,107
You don't punish a man
by givin' him what he wants.

760
01:12:14,982 --> 01:12:16,940
You just get me to the Council meeting.

761
01:12:17,023 --> 01:12:20,023
I wanna see their faces
while Moscow is still burnin'.

762
01:12:22,232 --> 01:12:24,482
(PEOPLE CHATTERING INDISTINCTLY)

763
01:12:49,190 --> 01:12:50,523
You, wait.

764
01:12:50,607 --> 01:12:52,148
Uh, yeah, that's not happening.

765
01:12:52,232 --> 01:12:53,232
Gravik.

766
01:12:59,940 --> 01:13:01,607
If I'm not out in an hour,

767
01:13:02,815 --> 01:13:04,023
shoot him in the head.

768
01:13:16,023 --> 01:13:17,648
Members of the Council.

769
01:13:19,273 --> 01:13:22,148
Seems someone didn't get
the suggested attire memo.

770
01:13:22,857 --> 01:13:26,565
Well, I also didn't get a formal
invitation, Mr. Secretary-General.

771
01:13:26,648 --> 01:13:28,773
But I'm sure
that was just a curious oversight.

772
01:13:31,773 --> 01:13:32,940
Madam Prime Minister.

773
01:13:35,857 --> 01:13:36,857
Hello, Shirley.

774
01:13:38,398 --> 01:13:42,773
I trust I speak for the group when I say,
we are all happy to have you with us.

775
01:13:42,857 --> 01:13:44,857
Please sit.

776
01:13:53,773 --> 01:13:55,107
GRAVIK: I see you,

777
01:13:55,190 --> 01:13:59,690
all dressed up in the man's finery,
drinking the man's wine.

778
01:14:00,273 --> 01:14:03,440
Playing the man's game,
using the man's fork and knife.

779
01:14:04,107 --> 01:14:06,232
Better to behave as a human than as a dog.

780
01:14:08,357 --> 01:14:09,565
Well, I quite like dogs.

781
01:14:11,107 --> 01:14:12,773
In fact, I prefer 'em.

782
01:14:13,732 --> 01:14:16,982
Dogs aren't hypocrites.
And they don't lie.

783
01:14:18,357 --> 01:14:20,648
They don't lock each other up in cages.

784
01:14:20,732 --> 01:14:22,898
They don't pimp, poison,

785
01:14:23,815 --> 01:14:27,690
and they don't go out of their way
to degrade and destroy their own habitat.

786
01:14:29,148 --> 01:14:31,232
A naive reading of human history.

787
01:14:32,398 --> 01:14:34,440
It's the only reading of human history.

788
01:14:35,898 --> 01:14:37,065
Are you done?

789
01:14:38,065 --> 01:14:40,607
Perhaps we should get on
with what we came here for.

790
01:14:40,690 --> 01:14:42,732
SHIRLEY: A prudent suggestion, sister.

791
01:14:43,690 --> 01:14:47,648
Recent acts of terror
in cities across the globe,

792
01:14:47,732 --> 01:14:50,315
most notably in Moscow,

793
01:14:50,398 --> 01:14:54,773
severely undermine the stability
that this Council seeks to preserve.

794
01:14:55,815 --> 01:15:00,023
The purpose of tonight
is to determine what punishment, if any,

795
01:15:00,107 --> 01:15:04,107
should be meted out on the individual
who has imperiled us all.

796
01:15:04,607 --> 01:15:07,565
You murdered over 2,000 innocent humans.

797
01:15:08,148 --> 01:15:09,148
Children.

798
01:15:09,232 --> 01:15:11,815
And yet,
you don't seem remotely remorseful.

799
01:15:11,898 --> 01:15:14,815
What the hell gives you the right
to disobey this council?

800
01:15:17,107 --> 01:15:18,523
What gives me the right?

801
01:15:21,940 --> 01:15:23,648
{\an8}(SPEAKS SKRULL LANGUAGE)

802
01:16:05,440 --> 01:16:07,065
(IN ENGLISH) I think it's a war.

803
01:16:07,940 --> 01:16:09,482
I think it's a war!

804
01:16:10,107 --> 01:16:11,107
Hmm?

805
01:16:11,190 --> 01:16:14,732
And unlike the last war each one of us
around this table fought in,

806
01:16:14,815 --> 01:16:16,232
I'm not gonna lose this one.

807
01:16:16,690 --> 01:16:18,982
Humans are doomed to self-destruction.

808
01:16:19,065 --> 01:16:22,815
Long before we arrived on this planet,
they were destined to consume themselves.

809
01:16:22,898 --> 01:16:25,982
So, for anyone flinching
at the thought of innocent deaths,

810
01:16:26,065 --> 01:16:31,273
let me assure you,
we're only hastening the inevitable.

811
01:16:32,773 --> 01:16:34,940
SERGIO: And what happens
if the Avengers return?

812
01:16:36,148 --> 01:16:37,815
You don't think I thought about that?

813
01:16:38,940 --> 01:16:40,315
Put your faith in me.

814
01:16:41,107 --> 01:16:44,773
And I promise,
your loyalty will be repaid.

815
01:16:48,732 --> 01:16:51,107
Well, Madam Prime Minister...

816
01:16:58,190 --> 01:17:01,107
We need to streamline
our chain of command.

817
01:17:01,190 --> 01:17:03,898
Democracy is fine for peacetime,
but whilst at war,

818
01:17:03,982 --> 01:17:07,648
we need a single commander
whose war power is total and unchecked.

819
01:17:07,732 --> 01:17:08,898
My God!

820
01:17:08,982 --> 01:17:13,773
Therefore, I nominate Gravik
to the post of Skrull General.

821
01:17:13,857 --> 01:17:14,857
SERGIO: Traitor!

822
01:17:14,940 --> 01:17:16,982
You were in on this with him
the entire time!

823
01:17:17,065 --> 01:17:18,940
Seat yourself down, Sergio.
I'm not done yet.

824
01:17:19,023 --> 01:17:21,773
Who do you think you're talking to?
I'm the commander of NATO.

825
01:17:21,857 --> 01:17:25,148
I can mobilize a million troops
at the snap of a... (GRUNTS)

826
01:17:26,648 --> 01:17:28,065
Shall I remove him, Madame?

827
01:17:28,690 --> 01:17:30,857
Oh, I don't think
he'll be any more trouble.

828
01:17:30,940 --> 01:17:31,982
(GAGS)

829
01:17:33,857 --> 01:17:34,857
(COUGHS)

830
01:17:36,023 --> 01:17:39,607
All those in favor of Gravik
as our new general...

831
01:17:41,732 --> 01:17:42,732
will submit.

832
01:18:08,482 --> 01:18:12,440
I fear each one of you
has forgotten our history.

833
01:18:13,232 --> 01:18:17,857
We did not end up homeless refugees
because we were unwilling to wage war.

834
01:18:18,565 --> 01:18:22,482
We ended up homeless refugees
because we were too willing.

835
01:18:24,440 --> 01:18:26,440
I do not support your coup.

836
01:18:27,482 --> 01:18:30,065
I will not support your war.

837
01:18:31,398 --> 01:18:33,190
And I do not submit.

838
01:18:35,273 --> 01:18:37,982
If I had another 100 like you,
I could take on the universe.

839
01:18:42,190 --> 01:18:45,857
You go in peace, sister.
You'll not be harmed.

840
01:19:19,565 --> 01:19:21,982
(CELL PHONE VIBRATING)

841
01:19:26,857 --> 01:19:28,898
- Shirley.
<i>- It's Gravik.</i>

842
01:19:28,982 --> 01:19:31,398
The Council just voted him General.

843
01:19:31,482 --> 01:19:34,482
He has control of our people
and our future.

844
01:19:34,565 --> 01:19:36,023
If there's anything I can do...

845
01:19:36,107 --> 01:19:40,107
Yeah, set up a meet
between me and Gravik. Public place.

846
01:19:40,190 --> 01:19:41,690
<i>Talos, he will kill you.</i>

847
01:19:41,773 --> 01:19:43,482
Yeah, thanks for the faith.

848
01:19:43,565 --> 01:19:46,273
<i>You don't understand.
Gravik has changed.</i>

849
01:19:46,357 --> 01:19:48,648
So have I. Soren's dead.

850
01:19:49,482 --> 01:19:50,482
<i>I know.</i>

851
01:19:50,565 --> 01:19:53,398
<i>But if you can't keep it together,
you will not walk out alive.</i>

852
01:19:53,482 --> 01:19:55,648
Shirley, set up the meet.

853
01:19:56,273 --> 01:19:59,148
Just tell him
I wanna talk about my daughter.

854
01:20:31,690 --> 01:20:33,690
(ALL CHEERING)

855
01:20:39,148 --> 01:20:40,523
Thank you, sir.

856
01:20:42,023 --> 01:20:44,023
Without you, this wouldn't be possible.

857
01:20:55,857 --> 01:20:57,607
(INDISTINCT)

858
01:21:10,523 --> 01:21:12,523
(CHEERING CONTINUES)

859
01:22:01,732 --> 01:22:02,898
You don't have it.

860
01:22:05,190 --> 01:22:06,315
Harvest wasn't there.

861
01:22:07,565 --> 01:22:09,065
ROSA: Then it's back to scavenging.

862
01:22:09,857 --> 01:22:12,440
Our DNA selection
remains extremely limited.

863
01:22:12,523 --> 01:22:14,148
PAGON: I'll send out teams.

864
01:22:14,232 --> 01:22:16,648
ROSA: I was told this phase
would be over.

865
01:22:17,648 --> 01:22:18,773
So was I.

866
01:22:20,148 --> 01:22:24,148
Gravik has given me multiple locations
for the Harvest, all of them empty.

867
01:22:24,815 --> 01:22:26,648
Our fearless leader isn't always right.

868
01:22:28,023 --> 01:22:29,565
Perhaps I misheard you.

869
01:22:29,648 --> 01:22:32,398
Do you need anything else, Dr. Dalton?

870
01:22:32,482 --> 01:22:34,815
Yes. Your absence.

871
01:22:47,815 --> 01:22:48,815
(ROSA SIGHS)

872
01:22:58,065 --> 01:23:01,815
REPORTER: In this stunning sign
of just how seriously it regards rumors

873
01:23:01,898 --> 01:23:04,232
of American involvement
in the Moscow attacks,

874
01:23:04,315 --> 01:23:07,732
the 27 EU heads of state,
plus the British Prime Minster

875
01:23:07,815 --> 01:23:10,607
have all but commanded Washington
to account for itself

876
01:23:10,690 --> 01:23:13,982
at this emergency security summit
here in London.

877
01:23:15,523 --> 01:23:16,523
MAN: Colonel?

878
01:23:19,148 --> 01:23:20,232
Colonel Rhodes?

879
01:23:22,232 --> 01:23:25,482
Colonel, are you denying
that two of your citizens,

880
01:23:25,565 --> 01:23:28,898
Mr. Nicholas Fury and Miss Maria Hill,

881
01:23:28,982 --> 01:23:32,565
were present in Moscow
at the scene of the attacks?

882
01:23:33,607 --> 01:23:37,898
We are aware of allegations
that Mr. Fury and Miss Hill

883
01:23:37,982 --> 01:23:39,273
may have traveled to Moscow.

884
01:23:39,357 --> 01:23:42,857
Which, if true, it would've been in
their capacity as private citizens, so...

885
01:23:43,482 --> 01:23:48,148
Do these photos suffice as confirmation
of that fact, Colonel Rhodes?

886
01:23:48,232 --> 01:23:49,523
(CHUCKLES)

887
01:23:49,607 --> 01:23:51,065
Respectfully, Prime Minister,

888
01:23:51,148 --> 01:23:54,732
I can't take the authenticity
of Russian-supplied photos at face value.

889
01:23:54,815 --> 01:23:56,773
However, I will be more than happy

890
01:23:56,857 --> 01:23:59,232
to have them analyzed
at our facilities at Langley.

891
01:23:59,315 --> 01:24:00,523
(SCOFFS)

892
01:24:02,982 --> 01:24:06,523
How do you explain
Mr. Fury's presence in Moscow?

893
01:24:06,607 --> 01:24:09,982
Uh, alleged. Alleged presence, madam.

894
01:24:10,065 --> 01:24:11,065
(WOMAN SCOFFS)

895
01:24:12,398 --> 01:24:14,440
If Slovakia rolls its eyes at me
one more time,

896
01:24:14,523 --> 01:24:16,732
I'm gonna put on the suit
and carpet bomb it.

897
01:24:16,815 --> 01:24:18,523
PAMELA: Why are you here, Colonel?

898
01:24:18,607 --> 01:24:20,273
You are not a Head of State.

899
01:24:21,398 --> 01:24:25,148
Surely, President Ritson
is aware of the seriousness

900
01:24:25,232 --> 01:24:28,440
with which his international partners
regard this allegation.

901
01:24:31,482 --> 01:24:34,857
Well, I'm here as a courtesy,
Madam Prime Minister.

902
01:24:34,940 --> 01:24:36,982
President Ritson has a pretty busy day job

903
01:24:37,065 --> 01:24:40,357
running the most powerful country
and military on the face of the planet.

904
01:24:40,440 --> 01:24:42,065
He doesn't just hop to when summoned.

905
01:24:42,148 --> 01:24:45,440
Not by France,
not by Italy, not by the UK.

906
01:24:46,065 --> 01:24:49,148
Now, while we are sensitive
to your concerns,

907
01:24:49,232 --> 01:24:52,482
until such time as you can present
an actual shred of evidence

908
01:24:52,565 --> 01:24:54,440
to back those concerns up,

909
01:24:54,523 --> 01:24:57,398
I'm afraid sensitivity
is all you're gonna be getting from us.

910
01:24:59,273 --> 01:25:00,273
All right?

911
01:25:00,815 --> 01:25:02,815
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

912
01:25:04,023 --> 01:25:06,023
(CELL PHONE VIBRATING)

913
01:25:09,773 --> 01:25:12,398
- Rhodes.
- FURY: <i>Nice suit. Armani?</i>

914
01:25:13,523 --> 01:25:15,065
(SIGHS) Brioni.

915
01:25:15,148 --> 01:25:16,148
(WHISPERS) Fury.

916
01:25:16,232 --> 01:25:18,440
<i>Pretty expensive for a government salary.</i>

917
01:25:18,523 --> 01:25:20,898
Yeah, well,
my other suit's made of titanium

918
01:25:20,982 --> 01:25:23,440
so this actually constitutes
considerable savings.

919
01:25:23,523 --> 01:25:25,398
<i>We need to meet. ASAP.</i>

920
01:25:25,482 --> 01:25:27,982
Great. Tell you what,
let me just finish mopping up

921
01:25:28,065 --> 01:25:31,440
this globe-sized bucket of steaming hot
kaka you tipped over yesterday

922
01:25:31,523 --> 01:25:33,440
and then, we can get a drink. Sound good?

923
01:25:33,523 --> 01:25:37,482
<i>You sound frustrated.
What's the matter? Croatia talking crap?</i>

924
01:25:37,565 --> 01:25:38,648
Slovakia.

925
01:25:39,232 --> 01:25:40,773
<i>Well, carpet-bomb their ass.</i>

926
01:25:41,565 --> 01:25:43,732
Burner's Tavern, one o'clock.

927
01:25:43,815 --> 01:25:47,690
Do me a favor and try not to pop off
a nuclear holocaust before you get there.

928
01:26:14,232 --> 01:26:15,648
(SIGHS)

929
01:26:18,482 --> 01:26:20,398
Should I be worried about poison?

930
01:26:21,065 --> 01:26:23,607
You should be worried
about spending the rest of your days

931
01:26:23,690 --> 01:26:25,565
in the Siberian retirement community.

932
01:26:25,648 --> 01:26:28,148
Yeah, don't let the relaxed ambiance
fool you.

933
01:26:28,732 --> 01:26:31,023
I'm this close to handing your ass
over to the Russians.

934
01:26:31,107 --> 01:26:33,148
Forgetting your rank here, Colonel Rhodes?

935
01:26:33,232 --> 01:26:35,648
You do not wanna be playing
"mine is bigger than yours"

936
01:26:35,732 --> 01:26:37,482
with job titles right now, Fury.

937
01:26:37,565 --> 01:26:40,315
Trust me, I'm the last friend you've got.

938
01:26:40,398 --> 01:26:42,357
Are the Russians
really tryin' to pin this on me?

939
01:26:42,440 --> 01:26:44,607
Your face is all over CCTV footage.

940
01:26:44,690 --> 01:26:47,190
I was there trying to stop the attack.

941
01:26:47,273 --> 01:26:51,232
Oh, well, excellent job at that,
by the way. 2,000 dead so far.

942
01:26:51,315 --> 01:26:53,940
Number will probably triple
once they clear all the rubble.

943
01:26:54,023 --> 01:26:56,648
Meaning you not only set the stage
for World War III,

944
01:26:56,732 --> 01:26:59,982
but you simultaneously flipped
all of our allies to Team Russia.

945
01:27:10,315 --> 01:27:12,690
How well do you know your security detail?

946
01:27:13,690 --> 01:27:16,398
I know they're catching bullets first
if I get shot at.

947
01:27:16,482 --> 01:27:19,482
(CHUCKLES) What do you mean
how much do I know about 'em?

948
01:27:19,565 --> 01:27:22,607
What if I told you they were all spies?

949
01:27:23,773 --> 01:27:25,315
Spies for who, the Russians?

950
01:27:26,107 --> 01:27:28,857
Well... non-state actors.

951
01:27:28,940 --> 01:27:32,232
You know, global reach,
borderless operations.

952
01:27:33,440 --> 01:27:35,273
- HYDRA?
- Yeah.

953
01:27:35,357 --> 01:27:40,107
If HYDRA was a bunch of green guys
who could shape-shift into your daddy.

954
01:27:44,315 --> 01:27:45,398
(CHUCKLES)

955
01:27:46,898 --> 01:27:48,065
(SIGHS)

956
01:27:49,357 --> 01:27:51,607
So, how long have you known about them?

957
01:27:53,732 --> 01:27:54,898
About 15 years ago,

958
01:27:54,982 --> 01:27:58,898
I was part of an eyes-only,
top-secret presentation.

959
01:27:58,982 --> 01:28:01,565
It was about
a shape-shifting alien species

960
01:28:01,648 --> 01:28:04,440
that had sent a few of its light ships
crashing down to Earth.

961
01:28:05,440 --> 01:28:06,690
The Pentagon was concerned

962
01:28:06,773 --> 01:28:10,773
that they might get into their heads
to invade us one day from the inside.

963
01:28:11,440 --> 01:28:14,732
That invasion is real. It's happened.

964
01:28:15,482 --> 01:28:17,732
That's... That's not possible.

965
01:28:17,815 --> 01:28:20,023
Yeah, that's what I thought, too,
but it's true.

966
01:28:20,107 --> 01:28:21,815
And here's the crazy part,

967
01:28:21,898 --> 01:28:25,732
we're being invaded and we can't even tell
who the invaders are.

968
01:28:25,815 --> 01:28:27,815
Moscow was just the beginning.

969
01:28:29,607 --> 01:28:31,065
Maybe we should call our friends.

970
01:28:31,148 --> 01:28:33,648
No, no, no, we can't jump the gun on that.

971
01:28:33,732 --> 01:28:36,273
You know, we get them
in a fight with the Skrulls

972
01:28:36,357 --> 01:28:37,607
and next thing you know,

973
01:28:37,690 --> 01:28:40,857
they find themselves duplicated
and turned into terrorists.

974
01:28:40,940 --> 01:28:42,065
Fury, this isn't...

975
01:28:42,148 --> 01:28:44,482
This is my war, Rhodey.

976
01:28:44,565 --> 01:28:46,357
I need you to back me on this.

977
01:28:46,773 --> 01:28:48,523
(SIGHS) I... I can't do it.

978
01:28:48,607 --> 01:28:50,023
Ain't no "can't" in our business.

979
01:28:50,107 --> 01:28:52,857
There's only what you can do
and what you will not do.

980
01:28:52,940 --> 01:28:55,690
You're right.
I should've said, I'm not doing it.

981
01:28:55,773 --> 01:28:57,773
I just spent
all the political capital I had

982
01:28:57,857 --> 01:29:00,107
in getting Maria Hill's body
back from the Russians.

983
01:29:00,190 --> 01:29:02,166
Are you really talking to me
about politics right now?

984
01:29:02,190 --> 01:29:05,357
I'm here as an envoy
of the United States government, Fury.

985
01:29:05,440 --> 01:29:06,565
The job is political.

986
01:29:06,648 --> 01:29:09,148
I remember when your job
was protecting the planet.

987
01:29:09,232 --> 01:29:12,398
We protect the planet
by protecting our seat at the table.

988
01:29:12,482 --> 01:29:15,023
Are you forgetting who helped you
get your seat at the table?

989
01:29:15,107 --> 01:29:16,982
Oh, so I owe you now? Is that it?

990
01:29:17,065 --> 01:29:19,190
We owe each other.

991
01:29:19,982 --> 01:29:23,648
Men who look like us don't get promoted
because of who our daddies know.

992
01:29:23,732 --> 01:29:26,482
Every ounce of power
we wrestle from the vice grip

993
01:29:26,565 --> 01:29:32,273
of the mediocre Alexander Pierces
who run this world was earned in blood.

994
01:29:32,357 --> 01:29:35,732
So let's make the power mean something.
Help a brother out.

995
01:29:36,398 --> 01:29:38,107
Car's outside, Colonel.

996
01:29:39,565 --> 01:29:41,773
Colonel Rhodes will let you know
when he's ready to go.

997
01:29:41,857 --> 01:29:43,357
RHODEY: The car is for you, Fury.

998
01:29:43,440 --> 01:29:46,232
They'll escort you outside,
then you're goin' to the airport.

999
01:29:46,315 --> 01:29:49,565
Oh. I'm sorry.
I didn't know I had travel plans.

1000
01:29:50,232 --> 01:29:51,773
I made 'em on your behalf.

1001
01:29:52,357 --> 01:29:54,166
Have you even listened
to a word that I've said?

1002
01:29:54,190 --> 01:29:57,523
Yeah, I have. The world is on the line.

1003
01:29:57,607 --> 01:30:00,315
The enemy is a million times
more dangerous than HYDRA,

1004
01:30:00,398 --> 01:30:02,273
but they can only be vanquished by you.

1005
01:30:02,357 --> 01:30:03,357
Alone.

1006
01:30:03,440 --> 01:30:06,773
And you want me to make the power
mean something by helpin' a brother out.

1007
01:30:06,857 --> 01:30:08,357
But you should know better than most.

1008
01:30:08,440 --> 01:30:13,107
The reason we wrestled this power
from mediocre men who don't look like us

1009
01:30:13,190 --> 01:30:16,398
was not simply to turn around
and hand it to mediocre men who do.

1010
01:30:16,482 --> 01:30:19,690
The point of this power
is to be uncompromising,

1011
01:30:19,773 --> 01:30:21,440
to be unsparing,

1012
01:30:21,523 --> 01:30:24,732
to be able to sit across
from a man we greatly admire,

1013
01:30:25,315 --> 01:30:30,023
with whom we share an entire professional,
personal, ancestral history with

1014
01:30:30,107 --> 01:30:33,482
and to tell him without any reservation,
that he's fired.

1015
01:30:34,773 --> 01:30:38,315
That's what this moment right here,
right now is about, Nick.

1016
01:30:39,065 --> 01:30:40,148
(SCOFFS)

1017
01:30:41,148 --> 01:30:42,232
(CHUCKLES)

1018
01:30:45,815 --> 01:30:47,440
(COUGHS)

1019
01:30:47,940 --> 01:30:51,023
They sent you to fire me?

1020
01:30:51,107 --> 01:30:54,273
Nobody sent me. I volunteered.

1021
01:30:54,357 --> 01:30:58,357
And not to put too fine a point on this,
but that mess that you created in Moscow

1022
01:30:58,440 --> 01:31:01,148
that resulted in getting
one of our best people murdered,

1023
01:31:01,232 --> 01:31:03,440
you earned all this smoke, brother.

1024
01:31:10,732 --> 01:31:11,773
Move.

1025
01:31:11,857 --> 01:31:14,898
- (GROANS)
- Are you seriously under the impression

1026
01:31:14,982 --> 01:31:19,232
that just because you strip me
of my titles, I relinquish my DNA?

1027
01:31:19,315 --> 01:31:20,315
Careful, Fury.

1028
01:31:21,398 --> 01:31:22,565
- (BONE CRACKS)
- (GROANS)

1029
01:31:29,523 --> 01:31:31,107
RHODEY: And you wonder why you're out.

1030
01:31:33,065 --> 01:31:34,273
I'm Nick Fury.

1031
01:31:35,732 --> 01:31:38,898
Even when I'm out, I'm in.

1032
01:31:48,690 --> 01:31:49,982
(WHEEZES)

1033
01:32:11,732 --> 01:32:13,148
{\an8}(SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

1034
01:32:13,232 --> 01:32:15,208
(IN ENGLISH) Yes,
and now that the door is unlocked,

1035
01:32:15,232 --> 01:32:17,023
what does that tell you
about me and doors?

1036
01:32:18,398 --> 01:32:19,565
Who are you?

1037
01:32:19,648 --> 01:32:21,607
I'm above your pay grade. Where is he?

1038
01:32:24,232 --> 01:32:25,315
Thank you.

1039
01:32:43,315 --> 01:32:44,315
{\an8}(SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

1040
01:32:45,773 --> 01:32:47,690
(IN ENGLISH) Where is your safe house?

1041
01:32:47,773 --> 01:32:49,666
- Speak!
- SONYA: Didn't your mother ever warn you

1042
01:32:49,690 --> 01:32:52,398
you could lose an eye
by beating your meat like that?

1043
01:32:52,482 --> 01:32:53,857
(LAUGHS SARCASTICALLY)

1044
01:32:54,607 --> 01:32:56,190
What are you doing here?

1045
01:32:56,273 --> 01:32:57,815
Oh, I'm taking over.

1046
01:33:05,690 --> 01:33:07,023
(MAN SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

1047
01:33:25,023 --> 01:33:28,940
(IN ENGLISH) I've thrown everything at him
and he hasn't said a word.

1048
01:33:29,023 --> 01:33:31,398
What makes you think
you can get him to speak?

1049
01:33:31,482 --> 01:33:33,065
Oh, I can be quite persuasive.

1050
01:33:33,690 --> 01:33:36,482
Oh, before I forget,
where is the escape hatch in this dump?

1051
01:33:36,565 --> 01:33:37,857
Why do you need to know that?

1052
01:33:37,940 --> 01:33:38,940
Oh, just a hunch.

1053
01:33:42,023 --> 01:33:44,607
Oh, wonderful. Okay, make yourself scarce.

1054
01:33:59,982 --> 01:34:01,440
MAN: What are you looking at?

1055
01:34:04,190 --> 01:34:07,857
Alone at last. Now, shall we do this
the easy way or the other way?

1056
01:34:08,523 --> 01:34:10,148
I'm gonna break these chains.

1057
01:34:10,232 --> 01:34:13,107
And then, I'm gonna break
every bone in your body.

1058
01:34:13,190 --> 01:34:15,232
(CHUCKLES) The other way it is.

1059
01:34:19,690 --> 01:34:20,815
(SCREAMING IN PAIN)

1060
01:34:23,273 --> 01:34:24,273
(GRUNTS)

1061
01:34:25,023 --> 01:34:26,023
Mmm.

1062
01:34:26,107 --> 01:34:29,982
Well, now that's confirmed,
let's party, shall we?

1063
01:34:30,065 --> 01:34:31,732
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1064
01:34:35,815 --> 01:34:36,815
(TYPING)

1065
01:34:54,648 --> 01:34:56,148
What are you doing in here?

1066
01:34:58,232 --> 01:35:00,440
Checking the progress
of our newest recruit.

1067
01:35:02,107 --> 01:35:04,023
He'll be ready for a face before long.

1068
01:35:09,273 --> 01:35:10,440
He's loyal.

1069
01:35:11,315 --> 01:35:12,315
GRAVIK: Loyal.

1070
01:35:14,315 --> 01:35:17,065
You know, I remember
when you first came to me, G'iah.

1071
01:35:18,565 --> 01:35:20,398
The daughter of a failed General.

1072
01:35:21,357 --> 01:35:25,773
I thought to myself, what kind of coward
sends his daughter to do what he wouldn't?

1073
01:35:25,857 --> 01:35:30,648
But you know, then I realized that kind of
coward just doesn't have it in him.

1074
01:35:39,065 --> 01:35:41,523
Our man on the inside located Brogan.

1075
01:35:45,523 --> 01:35:46,523
Let's go then.

1076
01:35:47,273 --> 01:35:50,273
You're wasting your time.
I'll never talk to you.

1077
01:35:50,357 --> 01:35:51,648
Well, that's very brave,

1078
01:35:51,732 --> 01:35:55,440
but everyone talks
when their blood starts to cook at 160°C.

1079
01:35:55,523 --> 01:35:57,148
It's a biochemical imperative.

1080
01:35:57,232 --> 01:35:59,857
The smart ones
start talking earlier than that.

1081
01:35:59,940 --> 01:36:01,273
You a smart one?

1082
01:36:01,357 --> 01:36:02,440
(GRUNTS)

1083
01:36:02,523 --> 01:36:03,940
Right, I didn't think so.

1084
01:36:04,857 --> 01:36:07,565
Go ahead, put it in my arm. I don't care.

1085
01:36:12,898 --> 01:36:13,982
(BROGAN GROANS)

1086
01:36:19,190 --> 01:36:21,190
(SIZZLING)

1087
01:36:22,857 --> 01:36:23,857
(GRUNTS)

1088
01:36:26,190 --> 01:36:27,190
(YELLS)

1089
01:36:44,357 --> 01:36:45,815
(SCREAMING IN PAIN)

1090
01:36:51,148 --> 01:36:53,482
SONYA: Tell me the location
of Gravik's compound.

1091
01:36:53,565 --> 01:36:56,482
I swear I know nothing. Please!

1092
01:36:56,565 --> 01:36:59,190
I'm afraid, sorry, dear heart,
I can't work with nothing.

1093
01:37:00,440 --> 01:37:03,690
I need to know where Gravik is,
and where he'll be.

1094
01:37:03,773 --> 01:37:07,107
I don't know, I swear.
Gravik keeps everything a secret.

1095
01:37:07,773 --> 01:37:09,357
And what secrets doesn't he keep?

1096
01:37:12,440 --> 01:37:13,732
He's building a machine.

1097
01:37:13,815 --> 01:37:15,023
What kind of machine?

1098
01:37:17,023 --> 01:37:18,690
I think it's to make us stronger.

1099
01:37:26,232 --> 01:37:27,352
GRAVIK: You wait in the car.

1100
01:37:27,398 --> 01:37:28,940
- Keep the engine running.
- Mmm-hmm.

1101
01:37:32,898 --> 01:37:33,982
Who's helping you?

1102
01:37:36,273 --> 01:37:37,440
I don't know what you mean.

1103
01:37:37,523 --> 01:37:39,315
Who's leading the science?

1104
01:37:39,398 --> 01:37:41,398
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1105
01:37:44,565 --> 01:37:45,898
Some married couple.

1106
01:37:47,023 --> 01:37:48,023
What's their name?

1107
01:37:50,690 --> 01:37:53,482
I can't, please. Gravik will kill me.

1108
01:37:54,732 --> 01:37:56,773
I'm terribly sorry,
but if I don't get a name,

1109
01:37:56,857 --> 01:37:59,148
- Gravik won't get the chance to kill you.
- (GROANS)

1110
01:38:02,940 --> 01:38:03,940
Please.

1111
01:38:05,690 --> 01:38:06,690
Dalton.

1112
01:38:08,607 --> 01:38:09,732
The name's Dalton.

1113
01:38:11,773 --> 01:38:14,023
You see,
that wasn't so terribly difficult, was it?

1114
01:38:15,857 --> 01:38:16,857
{\an8}(SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

1115
01:38:32,940 --> 01:38:33,940
(SILENCED GUNSHOT)

1116
01:38:44,065 --> 01:38:45,482
(MEN CHATTING INDISTINCTLY)

1117
01:39:00,482 --> 01:39:01,607
(MEN GRUNTING)

1118
01:39:07,648 --> 01:39:08,940
Sounds like your lift is here.

1119
01:39:10,065 --> 01:39:11,315
(GRUNTS)

1120
01:39:13,315 --> 01:39:15,607
Listen, I'm just gonna go
and check around back.

1121
01:39:16,565 --> 01:39:17,565
Cool. I'll come with.

1122
01:39:17,648 --> 01:39:20,232
No, no, no. You stay here.
They might come out with Brogan.

1123
01:39:21,273 --> 01:39:22,315
Yeah.

1124
01:39:22,398 --> 01:39:23,607
You're a smart lady, G'iah.

1125
01:39:51,065 --> 01:39:52,940
How very Dostoyevsky.

1126
01:39:55,190 --> 01:39:56,565
(MAN GRUNTING)

1127
01:40:00,065 --> 01:40:01,440
(SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

1128
01:40:06,190 --> 01:40:07,190
(GRUNTS)

1129
01:40:08,648 --> 01:40:09,648
(GROANS)

1130
01:40:31,565 --> 01:40:32,565
PAGON: Gotcha.

1131
01:40:34,565 --> 01:40:35,773
You're all right.

1132
01:40:35,857 --> 01:40:37,898
I've got him. Let's go.

1133
01:40:45,023 --> 01:40:46,190
What'd you tell 'em?

1134
01:40:47,482 --> 01:40:48,815
Nothin', just lies.

1135
01:40:50,440 --> 01:40:51,440
Nothin'?

1136
01:40:52,523 --> 01:40:53,940
Just lies?

1137
01:40:54,023 --> 01:40:55,273
That's all, I swear.

1138
01:41:06,398 --> 01:41:07,565
GRAVIK: Take him to the car.

1139
01:41:30,898 --> 01:41:32,190
- (BROGAN GRUNTS)
- Keep driving.

1140
01:41:35,357 --> 01:41:37,398
How did they find our safe house?

1141
01:41:40,482 --> 01:41:42,190
(BROGAN BREATHING RAGGEDLY)

1142
01:41:46,023 --> 01:41:47,398
(BROGAN PANTING)

1143
01:41:48,273 --> 01:41:49,315
(BROGAN GRUNTS)

1144
01:41:51,148 --> 01:41:52,690
(SIRENS WAILING)

1145
01:42:01,148 --> 01:42:02,148
GRAVIK: Pull over.

1146
01:42:12,648 --> 01:42:13,732
(GUN COCKING)

1147
01:42:16,357 --> 01:42:17,565
(BROGAN GRUNTING)

1148
01:42:27,607 --> 01:42:29,148
Did we make it home, Pagon?

1149
01:42:31,107 --> 01:42:32,315
Almost there, bro.

1150
01:42:37,690 --> 01:42:38,773
(BROGAN GRUNTS)

1151
01:42:47,190 --> 01:42:48,565
(BROGAN PANTING)

1152
01:42:59,023 --> 01:43:00,023
(GUNSHOT)

1153
01:43:00,482 --> 01:43:01,607
(BODY THUDS)

1154
01:43:47,357 --> 01:43:48,357
(GRUNTS)

1155
01:43:53,440 --> 01:43:54,482
(ENGINE STARTS)

1156
01:44:09,148 --> 01:44:11,148
(SOFT MUSIC PLAYING ON STEREO)

1157
01:44:45,315 --> 01:44:46,398
(SIGHS)

1158
01:45:01,357 --> 01:45:03,023
Aren't you forgetting something?

1159
01:45:21,232 --> 01:45:22,232
Better?

1160
01:45:25,482 --> 01:45:26,690
Almost.

1161
01:45:28,398 --> 01:45:30,523
("TRY A LITTLE TENDERNESS"
BY OTIS REDDING PLAYING)

1162
01:45:35,398 --> 01:45:40,857
<i>All you got to do is, man,
hold her when you wanna</i>

1163
01:45:40,940 --> 01:45:45,523
<i>Squeeze her, don't tease her,
never leave her</i>

1164
01:45:46,357 --> 01:45:52,523
<i>Get to her, got, got, got to try
a little tenderness, yeah, yeah</i>

1165
01:45:52,732 --> 01:45:55,690
<i>You got to know how to love her, man</i>

1166
01:45:55,773 --> 01:45:58,273
<i>Don't be surprised, man</i>

1167
01:45:58,357 --> 01:46:02,690
<i>You got to squeeze her,
don't tease her, never leave</i>

1168
01:46:02,773 --> 01:46:06,940
<i>You got to hold her,
brother, something, man</i>

1169
01:46:07,023 --> 01:46:10,315
<i>Try a little tenderness
yeah, yeah, yeah</i>

1170
01:46:10,648 --> 01:46:13,482
<i>You got to grab her gently, man</i>

1171
01:46:15,648 --> 01:46:17,273
<i>Don't bruise her, no, no</i>

1172
01:46:17,357 --> 01:46:21,523
<i>You got to love her, tease her,
don't squeeze her</i>

1173
01:46:21,607 --> 01:46:23,982
<i>You got to try, na na na na na</i>

1174
01:46:24,065 --> 01:46:27,857
<i>Try, try a little tenderness, yeah</i>

1175
01:46:27,940 --> 01:46:28,940
<i>Watch her groove</i>

1176
01:46:29,482 --> 01:46:32,482
<i>You got to know what to do, man</i>

1177
01:46:32,565 --> 01:46:33,898
<i>Take this advice</i>

1178
01:46:33,982 --> 01:46:37,940
<i>You gotta love, squeeze, don't tease</i>

1179
01:48:26,197 --> 01:48:41,197
<font color="#ff8040">{\an8}Downloaded From MoviesMod.org</font>

1180
01:48:32,760 --> 01:48:34,719
Fury, I'd like you to meet someone.

1181
01:48:36,219 --> 01:48:37,219
This is Gravik.

1182
01:48:39,094 --> 01:48:40,177
- (GUN FIRES)
- (GROANS)

1183
01:48:41,052 --> 01:48:42,260
(CROWD SCREAMING)

1184
01:48:42,635 --> 01:48:43,885
FURY: Gravik?

1185
01:48:44,219 --> 01:48:45,427
G'IAH: <i>You don't trust me.</i>

1186
01:48:47,844 --> 01:48:50,594
You're telling me
there's a million Skrulls

1187
01:48:50,719 --> 01:48:52,427
walking amongst us right now?

1188
01:48:52,510 --> 01:48:55,469
Have you lost your reptilian-ass mind?

1189
01:48:57,177 --> 01:48:59,885
SONYA: <i>Skrulls have infiltrated the ranks
of major world powers.</i>

1190
01:48:59,969 --> 01:49:01,049
DERRIK: <i>Where is the proof?</i>

1191
01:49:01,094 --> 01:49:04,094
I nominate Gravik
to the post of Skrull General.

1192
01:49:05,010 --> 01:49:07,385
They sent you to fire me?

1193
01:49:07,469 --> 01:49:08,635
I volunteered.

1194
01:49:08,719 --> 01:49:10,427
Set up a meet between me and Gravik.

1195
01:49:10,510 --> 01:49:11,760
Talos, he will kill you.

1196
01:49:11,844 --> 01:49:13,552
I wanna talk about my daughter.

1197
01:49:42,802 --> 01:49:44,969
PAGON: Everyone ready?
ZIRKSU: Uh-huh.

1198
01:49:46,927 --> 01:49:48,344
Do you think it'll work?

1199
01:49:51,094 --> 01:49:52,469
I mean, uh...

1200
01:49:52,552 --> 01:49:53,969
Bringing chaos?

1201
01:49:57,427 --> 01:49:59,635
Why did you join the resistance, Beto?

1202
01:50:01,844 --> 01:50:02,969
Um...

1203
01:50:03,802 --> 01:50:06,052
I did not want our people to keep running.

1204
01:50:15,177 --> 01:50:16,969
You joined the same reason I did.

1205
01:50:18,052 --> 01:50:22,302
Not fear of the past, faith in our future.

1206
01:50:24,219 --> 01:50:27,594
All faith is built on risk.

1207
01:50:31,885 --> 01:50:34,094
So that's what we have to take. Yeah?

1208
01:50:35,427 --> 01:50:36,719
Yeah.

1209
01:51:34,719 --> 01:51:35,719
GRAVIK: Ah!

1210
01:51:36,594 --> 01:51:38,135
Members of the Council.

1211
01:51:39,052 --> 01:51:41,094
Glad you could make it on short notice.

1212
01:51:43,677 --> 01:51:44,885
Now at the council meeting,

1213
01:51:44,969 --> 01:51:47,677
I told you I had a plan
for taking Earth as our own.

1214
01:51:48,385 --> 01:51:51,344
<i>I sent three operatives
to infiltrate the Royal Navy.</i>

1215
01:51:52,010 --> 01:51:53,469
Time to change.

1216
01:51:55,094 --> 01:51:58,427
GRAVIK: <i>And execute a strike
on a key United Nations target.</i>

1217
01:52:02,510 --> 01:52:04,969
<i>The heroes of Earth will react.</i>

1218
01:52:06,677 --> 01:52:09,635
<i>The only way we can counter that
and claim this planet as our home</i>

1219
01:52:10,677 --> 01:52:12,677
<i>is to become super ourselves.</i>

1220
01:52:13,719 --> 01:52:15,885
Now, we no longer just change faces.

1221
01:52:16,885 --> 01:52:18,177
We change powers.

1222
01:52:19,302 --> 01:52:22,552
We're gonna be uniquely programmed
weapons of mass destruction.

1223
01:52:23,635 --> 01:52:24,719
All of us.

1224
01:52:26,344 --> 01:52:27,469
Super Skrulls.

1225
01:52:28,719 --> 01:52:31,969
<i>Humans will be at all-out war
with each other within the week.</i>

1226
01:52:32,635 --> 01:52:36,302
<i>And while they're at each other's throats,
we're gonna break their backs.</i>

1227
01:52:39,927 --> 01:52:44,260
GRAVIK: <i>I invite you to join me
in the extinction of the human race.</i>

1228
01:54:50,969 --> 01:54:52,594
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

1229
01:55:13,135 --> 01:55:15,052
- (FURY SIGHS)
- Coffee?

1230
01:55:15,802 --> 01:55:17,052
Yes, please, black.

1231
01:55:24,260 --> 01:55:25,594
Looking for someone?

1232
01:55:27,844 --> 01:55:28,844
Uh, yes, I am.

1233
01:55:30,552 --> 01:55:31,844
What does she look like?

1234
01:55:33,469 --> 01:55:35,760
That depends
on what day of the week it is.

1235
01:55:39,177 --> 01:55:40,927
Wanna sit here while you wait?

1236
01:55:43,927 --> 01:55:46,469
Well... That...

1237
01:55:47,969 --> 01:55:50,010
That might send the wrong message.

1238
01:55:52,010 --> 01:55:53,260
She won't mind.

1239
01:55:57,219 --> 01:55:58,760
Varra?

1240
01:56:02,052 --> 01:56:05,052
VARRA: This should put Dreykov's men
on their heels.

1241
01:56:07,510 --> 01:56:09,385
Looks like you already have.

1242
01:56:15,260 --> 01:56:17,719
This new face of yours is...

1243
01:56:18,385 --> 01:56:19,427
Beautiful?

1244
01:56:19,885 --> 01:56:21,344
(CHUCKLES)

1245
01:56:23,052 --> 01:56:24,177
I agree.

1246
01:56:26,677 --> 01:56:27,844
FURY: Who is she?

1247
01:56:28,635 --> 01:56:30,385
Well, that depends on where this goes.

1248
01:56:30,469 --> 01:56:31,760
No, no, no, no, no.

1249
01:56:31,885 --> 01:56:33,260
There's a rule that, you know,

1250
01:56:33,344 --> 01:56:35,635
commander of station
and operatives cannot be...

1251
01:56:35,719 --> 01:56:37,760
Our unit doesn't exist, Fury.

1252
01:56:39,135 --> 01:56:40,802
That means I don't work for you.

1253
01:56:43,469 --> 01:56:46,302
- Well, that's an intriguing possibility.
- (CHUCKLES)

1254
01:56:51,302 --> 01:56:54,219
STEARNS ON TV: <i>Does anyone out there
seriously trust our leaders?</i>

1255
01:56:54,302 --> 01:56:55,385
<i>I sure don't.</i>

1256
01:56:55,469 --> 01:56:58,094
<i>Load your guns and make sure
you got enough food and water</i>

1257
01:56:58,219 --> 01:57:01,927
<i>because that, my friends,
looks a hell of a lot like World War III.</i>

1258
01:57:02,927 --> 01:57:04,927
How can you watch that poison?

1259
01:57:05,010 --> 01:57:07,385
Even a broken clock's right twice a day.

1260
01:57:07,469 --> 01:57:09,427
(CHUCKLES) Good morning.

1261
01:57:09,510 --> 01:57:10,760
Morning!

1262
01:57:14,552 --> 01:57:15,552
FURY: Mmm! Mmm!

1263
01:57:15,635 --> 01:57:18,927
Those eggs supposed to be soft
or hard boiled?

1264
01:57:19,552 --> 01:57:20,802
Poached.

1265
01:57:21,344 --> 01:57:23,177
(BOTH CHUCKLE)

1266
01:57:23,552 --> 01:57:26,760
I forgot.
Things cook differently up in space.

1267
01:57:29,260 --> 01:57:31,302
Whoa. Thank you.

1268
01:57:33,469 --> 01:57:36,844
Do I dare ask what calamity
must have transpired

1269
01:57:36,927 --> 01:57:38,844
to bring you home, to me?

1270
01:57:39,969 --> 01:57:41,927
It has been years.

1271
01:57:43,177 --> 01:57:46,969
If you want me to apologize
for being gone, Scilla, just say so.

1272
01:57:47,427 --> 01:57:49,260
Darling, you are Nick Fury.

1273
01:57:50,052 --> 01:57:54,552
I never harbored any illusions
about the necessity of you going away.

1274
01:57:55,927 --> 01:57:57,427
But staying away,

1275
01:57:57,969 --> 01:57:59,344
that leaves a mark.

1276
01:58:04,135 --> 01:58:05,469
(MUG THUDS ON TABLE)

1277
01:58:05,802 --> 01:58:07,094
I retired.

1278
01:58:10,635 --> 01:58:11,635
(FURY SIGHS)

1279
01:58:11,719 --> 01:58:13,427
Any plans for the downtime?

1280
01:58:14,177 --> 01:58:16,635
Well, you know,
I never cared much for golf, so...

1281
01:58:17,844 --> 01:58:21,344
I'm thinking I may take up revenge.

1282
01:58:28,760 --> 01:58:31,510
You been in touch with Gravik
while I was gone?

1283
01:58:33,052 --> 01:58:36,219
- And why are you asking me that?
- 'Cause I just need to be sure.

1284
01:58:36,302 --> 01:58:37,635
About what?

1285
01:58:38,677 --> 01:58:40,010
Who you've become

1286
01:58:42,385 --> 01:58:43,677
while I was gone.

1287
01:58:44,427 --> 01:58:47,219
I became a widow in your absence.

1288
01:58:48,760 --> 01:58:52,135
I wept on your pillow every night.
I grieved for you.

1289
01:58:53,969 --> 01:58:57,052
And just when I thought
I had gotten past the heartbreak,

1290
01:58:57,552 --> 01:58:59,010
you came back in the Blip.

1291
01:59:00,094 --> 01:59:03,510
And silly me, I thought we were
going to undo all the pain together.

1292
01:59:05,135 --> 01:59:07,677
Go back to the way we were, but no,

1293
01:59:09,885 --> 01:59:11,885
you just up and vanished again.

1294
01:59:12,135 --> 01:59:14,302
Only this time it was voluntary.

1295
01:59:15,719 --> 01:59:21,219
So if you're interested in who I became
in your second absence,

1296
01:59:22,135 --> 01:59:23,469
I became me.

1297
01:59:25,177 --> 01:59:26,802
The me I was before you.

1298
01:59:28,219 --> 01:59:31,177
What other choice was there
when you kept disappearing

1299
01:59:31,260 --> 01:59:33,844
as if you were never really here
in the first place?

1300
01:59:34,302 --> 01:59:36,302
(CELL PHONE VIBRATING)

1301
01:59:41,135 --> 01:59:42,760
Don't ignore it because of me.

1302
01:59:49,844 --> 01:59:51,677
(MAN ON PHONE SPEAKING)

1303
01:59:51,760 --> 01:59:54,469
I don't have that information
at hand right now.

1304
01:59:57,552 --> 01:59:58,844
You too, take care.

1305
02:00:00,635 --> 02:00:01,635
Something important?

1306
02:00:02,094 --> 02:00:03,094
Nope.

1307
02:00:26,385 --> 02:00:27,760
(G'IAH CLEARS THROAT)

1308
02:00:30,177 --> 02:00:31,927
What is it? What's happened?

1309
02:00:33,260 --> 02:00:34,719
(EXHALES)

1310
02:00:37,594 --> 02:00:38,594
Brogan.

1311
02:00:41,760 --> 02:00:42,969
What about him?

1312
02:00:43,469 --> 02:00:47,510
Well, someone told the cops
where we were headed,

1313
02:00:48,760 --> 02:00:50,052
and only we knew that.

1314
02:00:50,510 --> 02:00:54,302
It was me, you, Pagon and Beto in the car.

1315
02:00:55,844 --> 02:00:58,844
It's hard for Brogan to confess
to something he didn't know.

1316
02:01:00,802 --> 02:01:01,927
Not so hard.

1317
02:01:02,427 --> 02:01:03,427
Oh, yeah?

1318
02:01:03,969 --> 02:01:05,010
How'd you figure?

1319
02:01:05,969 --> 02:01:07,635
Brogan under torture.

1320
02:01:11,427 --> 02:01:14,135
I'd imagine when they asked him
where they could find you,

1321
02:01:14,219 --> 02:01:17,177
he was forced to make an educated guess.

1322
02:01:20,552 --> 02:01:21,719
Is that what you'd do?

1323
02:01:22,844 --> 02:01:23,885
I'd lie.

1324
02:01:24,802 --> 02:01:25,885
I'm a good liar.

1325
02:01:26,969 --> 02:01:27,969
(CHUCKLES)

1326
02:01:28,635 --> 02:01:29,677
Okay.

1327
02:01:33,177 --> 02:01:34,469
It was Brogan.

1328
02:01:35,260 --> 02:01:36,885
He was weaker than you thought.

1329
02:01:49,969 --> 02:01:51,010
All right.

1330
02:01:53,344 --> 02:01:54,927
See you tomorrow. Early.

1331
02:01:55,635 --> 02:01:56,760
You're coming with me.

1332
02:02:28,469 --> 02:02:30,344
GRAVIK: Your father called for a parley.

1333
02:02:32,385 --> 02:02:34,302
Apparently we're meeting about you.

1334
02:02:39,094 --> 02:02:40,927
(CELL PHONE VIBRATING)

1335
02:02:44,302 --> 02:02:45,302
Yeah.

1336
02:02:48,802 --> 02:02:50,135
Right on schedule.

1337
02:02:50,427 --> 02:02:54,719
The UN plane will be
at <i>Neptune's</i> coordinates, 2200 hours.

1338
02:03:00,635 --> 02:03:02,635
(PEOPLE CHATTERING INDISTINCTLY)

1339
02:03:39,802 --> 02:03:41,052
It's remarkable, innit?

1340
02:03:42,469 --> 02:03:45,802
Gathering up all these big men
for one painting.

1341
02:03:47,052 --> 02:03:51,510
<i>Statesmen of World War I.</i>
That's what it's called.

1342
02:03:51,594 --> 02:03:54,677
I mean, it just sums up the whole thing
pretty nice, I'd say.

1343
02:03:55,469 --> 02:03:56,969
Which whole thing is that?

1344
02:03:57,594 --> 02:04:01,927
You know, the difference
between statesmen and soldiers.

1345
02:04:02,260 --> 02:04:05,302
You see, 'cause one lot spends the war
posing for pictures,

1346
02:04:05,385 --> 02:04:07,219
while the other does all the killing

1347
02:04:07,635 --> 02:04:08,635
and the dying.

1348
02:04:08,719 --> 02:04:11,510
I mean, look at the fat
smug smile on his face.

1349
02:04:12,344 --> 02:04:13,594
You ask me, Talos,

1350
02:04:13,677 --> 02:04:17,594
choice between having my story told
in ink and oil paint

1351
02:04:18,094 --> 02:04:19,969
or having it written in blood,

1352
02:04:20,635 --> 02:04:24,802
I choose blood all day long.

1353
02:04:25,885 --> 02:04:28,802
Yours and everyone else's. Huh?

1354
02:04:29,635 --> 02:04:30,802
Yeah.

1355
02:04:31,177 --> 02:04:32,219
Brave.

1356
02:04:32,719 --> 02:04:35,177
You asked for parley,
so let's parley, shall we?

1357
02:04:35,260 --> 02:04:36,510
Come on.

1358
02:04:46,677 --> 02:04:47,885
Thank you, love.

1359
02:05:05,052 --> 02:05:07,052
Why don't you just get an empty cup?

1360
02:05:08,469 --> 02:05:10,719
I like a little bit of espresso
with my sugar.

1361
02:05:12,385 --> 02:05:13,552
You want some?

1362
02:05:14,177 --> 02:05:18,302
What I want is for you to stand down
and stop murdering innocent humans.

1363
02:05:18,802 --> 02:05:21,010
You know, I would be doing us both a favor

1364
02:05:21,260 --> 02:05:23,802
if I just put you
out of your misery right here.

1365
02:05:24,844 --> 02:05:27,677
You want an honor meeting?
Mate, go ahead, say the word.

1366
02:05:28,219 --> 02:05:29,219
An honor meeting?

1367
02:05:29,719 --> 02:05:31,677
Well, it wouldn't be proper, would it?

1368
02:05:31,802 --> 02:05:33,969
A general challenging his subordinate
to knives.

1369
02:05:34,969 --> 02:05:37,177
Are you honestly puzzled
as to why the Council

1370
02:05:37,260 --> 02:05:39,510
would prefer me as general
over the likes of you?

1371
02:05:39,635 --> 02:05:42,302
G'iah's in the car. Wanna come say hello?

1372
02:05:42,719 --> 02:05:46,469
You wanna be very, very careful now.

1373
02:05:47,094 --> 02:05:48,219
You should be grateful

1374
02:05:48,302 --> 02:05:51,094
that I haven't sent her back to you
in a body bag yet.

1375
02:06:15,802 --> 02:06:17,802
That's what this is all about, isn't it?

1376
02:06:17,885 --> 02:06:21,177
You're gonna take our people
to the edge of extinction

1377
02:06:21,260 --> 02:06:22,510
with the war with the humans.

1378
02:06:22,594 --> 02:06:24,469
All these miscreants know

1379
02:06:25,802 --> 02:06:26,927
is murder.

1380
02:06:28,469 --> 02:06:30,385
Look how they treat each other.

1381
02:06:30,469 --> 02:06:31,927
That's what's gonna happen.

1382
02:06:32,760 --> 02:06:34,302
We're gonna murder them all.

1383
02:06:34,719 --> 02:06:38,885
You don't understand
the first thing about humans.

1384
02:06:40,844 --> 02:06:43,302
They're at their most formidable

1385
02:06:44,594 --> 02:06:46,177
when they're threatened

1386
02:06:47,927 --> 02:06:49,719
by a common foe.

1387
02:06:50,385 --> 02:06:51,802
Have you forgotten how we fight?

1388
02:06:51,885 --> 02:06:53,010
You think I'll let you

1389
02:06:53,094 --> 02:06:56,469
continue this war
under the cover of anonymity,

1390
02:06:56,552 --> 02:06:57,885
you're very much mistaken.

1391
02:06:57,969 --> 02:07:01,302
I'm gonna tell every army on Earth
who it is that's attacking them.

1392
02:07:01,385 --> 02:07:03,219
You'll lose the element of surprise.

1393
02:07:03,302 --> 02:07:06,594
You and your rebels will be put down
like the rabid dogs you are.

1394
02:07:06,677 --> 02:07:09,302
Then you'll be the author
of our people's extermination.

1395
02:07:09,385 --> 02:07:11,302
And that's where you're wrong,
because you see,

1396
02:07:11,427 --> 02:07:15,177
they will see the difference between us

1397
02:07:15,260 --> 02:07:17,594
because we will show them,

1398
02:07:17,719 --> 02:07:22,594
we who haven't been infected
by your sickness.

1399
02:07:23,635 --> 02:07:25,427
So, then, G'iah stays with me then, is it?

1400
02:07:28,677 --> 02:07:31,844
Now, until the end of time,

1401
02:07:32,510 --> 02:07:34,719
my daughter's name
stays out of your mouth.

1402
02:07:36,427 --> 02:07:37,635
(STRAINS)

1403
02:07:38,135 --> 02:07:39,344
You got it?

1404
02:08:00,552 --> 02:08:02,177
- I'm sorry.
- No, I am.

1405
02:08:03,760 --> 02:08:07,219
- I believe this is yours.
- Thank you.

1406
02:09:10,969 --> 02:09:13,177
You really gonna eat
that plate of dog food?

1407
02:09:16,635 --> 02:09:19,219
I was, mate. I just lost my appetite.

1408
02:09:19,302 --> 02:09:20,594
Oh, that's a first.

1409
02:09:21,552 --> 02:09:22,760
(SCOFFS)

1410
02:09:23,969 --> 02:09:26,135
You really are shameless, aren't you?

1411
02:09:26,552 --> 02:09:29,385
Anyone that could say
what you said to me yesterday,

1412
02:09:30,177 --> 02:09:33,135
have the balls to come up in here
and ask me for help?

1413
02:09:33,219 --> 02:09:34,594
I didn't ask you for help.

1414
02:09:35,010 --> 02:09:37,344
What, are you here to have
an English breakfast, mate,

1415
02:09:37,427 --> 02:09:39,844
or are you here to inquire
after my well-being?

1416
02:09:39,927 --> 02:09:43,260
No, I think it's a pretty safe bet
you ain't here for that, right? Hmm?

1417
02:09:43,344 --> 02:09:45,094
Look, look, look, look.

1418
02:09:45,219 --> 02:09:49,177
I got a lead on a rebel Skrull
that's high up in the U.S. government,

1419
02:09:49,260 --> 02:09:51,594
- and he's in London right now.
- And?

1420
02:09:51,927 --> 02:09:53,135
And?

1421
02:09:53,219 --> 02:09:55,552
Yeah, and what can I do for you?

1422
02:09:55,844 --> 02:09:57,427
How can I help you, my friend?

1423
02:09:58,260 --> 02:09:59,427
I just told you.

1424
02:09:59,510 --> 02:10:00,719
No, you told me

1425
02:10:00,802 --> 02:10:04,344
that you've got a line on a Skrull
that's up in the U.S. government and...

1426
02:10:04,427 --> 02:10:08,177
That it's understood
that you think that implies

1427
02:10:08,260 --> 02:10:10,510
that I should just sort of leap up

1428
02:10:10,594 --> 02:10:13,052
and take this opportunity
to just help you, like that.

1429
02:10:13,469 --> 02:10:19,427
Those days are gone, so I'm gonna
need you to, you know, use your words.

1430
02:10:20,219 --> 02:10:21,594
Say the words.

1431
02:10:22,594 --> 02:10:24,219
Say what words?

1432
02:10:26,219 --> 02:10:27,469
"Help me, Talos,

1433
02:10:28,302 --> 02:10:30,469
"'cause I'm useless without you."

1434
02:10:47,385 --> 02:10:48,802
(FURY SIGHS)

1435
02:10:50,969 --> 02:10:52,802
Help me, Talos,

1436
02:10:53,219 --> 02:10:55,927
'cause I am useless without you.

1437
02:11:11,969 --> 02:11:14,302
TALOS: G'iah handed off intel,
used a burner phone.

1438
02:11:14,969 --> 02:11:16,219
Brave girl.

1439
02:11:16,677 --> 02:11:18,885
Yeah. Her mum. Good role model.

1440
02:11:20,677 --> 02:11:23,427
<i>Neptune</i> is a British sub.
I know who to call.

1441
02:11:25,094 --> 02:11:26,427
(PHONE RINGING)

1442
02:11:28,385 --> 02:11:30,552
Whoever this is,
you shouldn't have this number.

1443
02:11:30,635 --> 02:11:33,635
FURY: <i>What do you know about</i>
<i>a British submarine called</i> Neptune?

1444
02:11:33,760 --> 02:11:35,302
First, I want an apology.

1445
02:11:35,385 --> 02:11:37,594
<i>I just gave away
the only one of those I had today.</i>

1446
02:11:37,677 --> 02:11:39,510
Well, you'll have to double down,

1447
02:11:39,594 --> 02:11:44,219
'cause you rather rudely attached
a nasty bug to my beloved Hoot.

1448
02:11:44,302 --> 02:11:46,219
<i>Tell me that's not the name
of that owl clock.</i>

1449
02:11:46,344 --> 02:11:49,552
No, not anymore. Has a new name now.
Nicholas Fury.

1450
02:11:50,219 --> 02:11:52,510
He has a rather
dashing little eye patch now.

1451
02:11:52,927 --> 02:11:55,469
<i>I'm serious, Sonya.
I have it on good authority.</i>

1452
02:11:55,552 --> 02:11:58,135
Neptune <i>is planning to launch</i>
<i>on the UN Delegation.</i>

1453
02:11:58,219 --> 02:12:00,094
<i>That would mean World War III.</i>

1454
02:12:00,635 --> 02:12:03,135
<i>Well, why would they
do something silly like that?</i>

1455
02:12:03,510 --> 02:12:06,510
Because at least one of Gravik's rebels
has infiltrated Command.

1456
02:12:06,594 --> 02:12:07,635
<i>Can you make the call?</i>

1457
02:12:07,719 --> 02:12:09,927
Unfortunately,
I'm dealing with my own infiltration

1458
02:12:10,010 --> 02:12:11,344
at the moment.

1459
02:12:11,427 --> 02:12:13,594
Somebody leaked the location
of the butcher's shop

1460
02:12:13,677 --> 02:12:16,510
when I was doing some of my best work,
so my hands are tied.

1461
02:12:16,635 --> 02:12:18,302
<i>Loose enough to get the captain's name?</i>

1462
02:12:18,802 --> 02:12:22,094
<i>- His name is Commodore Robert Fairbanks.</i>
- Bob!

1463
02:12:22,177 --> 02:12:24,510
- Can I get a photo and address?
<i>- Absolutely.</i>

1464
02:12:24,594 --> 02:12:27,344
<i>- Shall I tell him you're on your way?</i>
- Yeah. Tell him that.

1465
02:12:27,510 --> 02:12:28,969
(CHUCKLES)

1466
02:12:29,552 --> 02:12:30,552
(SIGHS)

1467
02:12:31,052 --> 02:12:32,052
(BEEPS)

1468
02:12:34,385 --> 02:12:35,385
Portsmouth.

1469
02:12:35,802 --> 02:12:38,510
That's where Naval Command HQ is.

1470
02:12:44,219 --> 02:12:48,385
You know what?
I don't get the whole dog thing.

1471
02:12:48,802 --> 02:12:51,510
What's to get?
Dogs are man's best friend.

1472
02:12:52,552 --> 02:12:54,760
But I mean, come on, look at that.

1473
02:12:55,260 --> 02:12:59,177
I mean, just name me
one other interspecies relationship

1474
02:12:59,260 --> 02:13:02,844
where it's acceptable
to clean up the other guy's poop.

1475
02:13:03,510 --> 02:13:06,510
I've been cleaning up your poop
for the last 30-some years.

1476
02:13:07,927 --> 02:13:09,135
Oh, that's rich.

1477
02:13:09,219 --> 02:13:12,094
Ah, the truth's a mother dog, right?

1478
02:13:12,219 --> 02:13:14,594
(BOTH LAUGH)

1479
02:13:15,760 --> 02:13:17,510
That's really what you think?

1480
02:13:17,594 --> 02:13:19,802
That the whole time
we've known each other,

1481
02:13:19,885 --> 02:13:21,760
you've been cleaning up my mess?

1482
02:13:21,844 --> 02:13:24,552
- You got a different take on it?
- Oh, well, let's see.

1483
02:13:24,927 --> 02:13:26,719
When I came here in 1995,

1484
02:13:26,802 --> 02:13:31,177
you were just a benchwarming nobody
in a dumpy field office in S.H.I.E.L.D.

1485
02:13:31,260 --> 02:13:32,344
Benchwarming?

1486
02:13:32,510 --> 02:13:34,760
What, do you have
a different take on this?

1487
02:13:35,260 --> 02:13:37,510
I was ascending the ranks.

1488
02:13:38,260 --> 02:13:41,344
You didn't start ascending the ranks

1489
02:13:41,427 --> 02:13:47,052
until me and 19 of my people
signed on as your invisible spy network.

1490
02:13:47,469 --> 02:13:51,302
You know, we fed you more dirt and intel

1491
02:13:51,510 --> 02:13:55,802
than you could've uncovered
on your own in a lifetime, so please.

1492
02:13:56,010 --> 02:14:00,469
I mean, every time you were promoted
inside S.H.I.E.L.D., we did that.

1493
02:14:01,219 --> 02:14:04,760
Every terror attack you prevented,
we did that.

1494
02:14:05,344 --> 02:14:09,885
Every enemy you sabotaged
and ally you leveraged with dirt

1495
02:14:09,969 --> 02:14:13,510
no one else in the world had access to,
we did that.

1496
02:14:14,760 --> 02:14:18,594
You're a smart and capable guy, Fury.
Nobody questions that.

1497
02:14:19,260 --> 02:14:20,677
But you've gotta admit,

1498
02:14:21,219 --> 02:14:24,552
your life got a hell of a lot more charmed
once I came into it.

1499
02:14:24,844 --> 02:14:26,302
And do you know something?

1500
02:14:26,677 --> 02:14:29,552
I don't even need to hear
a bloody thank you from you.

1501
02:14:30,219 --> 02:14:31,594
It was my pleasure, mate.

1502
02:14:32,594 --> 02:14:33,719
Least you can do

1503
02:14:35,010 --> 02:14:36,594
is not rewrite history

1504
02:14:36,927 --> 02:14:40,177
when the guy who helped write it
with you the first time

1505
02:14:40,510 --> 02:14:42,010
is sitting right next to you.

1506
02:14:42,094 --> 02:14:43,094
(ENGINE STOPS)

1507
02:14:43,177 --> 02:14:45,344
- What'd you stop for?
- We're here.

1508
02:14:46,260 --> 02:14:47,469
- At Bob's?
- Yeah, Bob.

1509
02:14:47,594 --> 02:14:50,010
Remember Bob?
The guy that'll launch a nuclear attack?

1510
02:14:50,094 --> 02:14:52,010
All right, I'm sorry.
I didn't realize that.

1511
02:14:52,094 --> 02:14:56,052
No, that's 'cause you were too busy
riding the "we did that" wave.

1512
02:14:56,635 --> 02:14:58,760
You got any more abuse
you wanna hurl my way?

1513
02:14:58,844 --> 02:15:01,552
Or are you ready to go in here
and take care of Bob?

1514
02:15:01,635 --> 02:15:04,469
And then I get to say, "We did that."

1515
02:15:05,885 --> 02:15:07,052
We can do that.

1516
02:15:16,469 --> 02:15:17,469
Sir.

1517
02:15:18,094 --> 02:15:20,010
Sorry. I didn't know you stepped out.

1518
02:15:20,094 --> 02:15:22,719
I needed a break
from the old ball and chain.

1519
02:15:22,802 --> 02:15:23,969
I can empathize, sir.

1520
02:15:24,469 --> 02:15:26,094
Don't let her hear you say that.

1521
02:15:33,594 --> 02:15:35,052
TALOS ON EARPIECE: <i>You in position?</i>

1522
02:15:35,135 --> 02:15:37,010
Worry about your own damn self.

1523
02:15:37,719 --> 02:15:39,344
<i>Do me a favor, Fury.</i>

1524
02:15:40,010 --> 02:15:41,094
Don't ever change.

1525
02:15:44,219 --> 02:15:46,344
- Sir, I just left you...
- Shit.

1526
02:15:47,594 --> 02:15:49,010
(SCREAMS)

1527
02:15:51,635 --> 02:15:53,677
- TALOS: <i>I'm blown.</i>
- Yeah, I see.

1528
02:15:55,010 --> 02:15:56,594
(BOTH GROAN)

1529
02:16:24,594 --> 02:16:25,677
Come in, Talos.

1530
02:16:26,219 --> 02:16:29,760
TALOS: <i>Sorry, Nick.
I was busy kicking Bob's ass.</i>

1531
02:16:29,927 --> 02:16:32,385
<i>Second floor. Last door down the hall.</i>

1532
02:16:33,010 --> 02:16:34,052
Copy that.

1533
02:16:50,594 --> 02:16:53,927
Nobody calls me Nick, Bob.

1534
02:16:54,385 --> 02:16:55,719
Zachary.

1535
02:16:55,802 --> 02:16:57,052
(TALOS GRUNTS)

1536
02:16:57,177 --> 02:16:58,177
ZACHARY: Dad?

1537
02:16:59,677 --> 02:17:01,052
(WHIMPERS)

1538
02:17:02,969 --> 02:17:04,010
Daddy?

1539
02:17:05,094 --> 02:17:07,927
I'll let him go when you let my son go.

1540
02:17:08,594 --> 02:17:11,635
This is not a negotiation, Bob.

1541
02:17:13,094 --> 02:17:14,302
(SIGHS)

1542
02:17:20,177 --> 02:17:21,385
(GRUNTS)

1543
02:17:25,594 --> 02:17:26,885
Find something to tie them up?

1544
02:17:27,844 --> 02:17:29,302
Sure thing, boss.

1545
02:17:30,677 --> 02:17:32,427
"Thanks for saving my life, Fury."

1546
02:17:32,719 --> 02:17:34,760
"No problem, Talos. Any time."

1547
02:17:36,219 --> 02:17:38,552
What you working on over there, Bob?

1548
02:17:50,510 --> 02:17:53,802
- MAN 1: Forty-five degrees right.
- MAN 2: to four zero feet.

1549
02:17:54,469 --> 02:17:57,177
MAN 1: Standby. Uh, ready one.

1550
02:17:58,094 --> 02:17:59,885
CAPTAIN: This has to be a mistake.

1551
02:18:00,885 --> 02:18:04,469
The message has been authenticated,
Captain. You are obliged to strike.

1552
02:18:04,552 --> 02:18:06,427
MAN 1: I'm at a 50 mile radius.

1553
02:18:13,469 --> 02:18:18,594
Here you go. Take a sip of this.
It's gonna help calm your nerves. Come on.

1554
02:18:21,510 --> 02:18:23,219
Are you gonna kill my dad?

1555
02:18:24,594 --> 02:18:27,552
I just need your dad
to do the right thing. Come on.

1556
02:18:39,844 --> 02:18:42,552
I can't seem to get old Bob here
to listen to reason.

1557
02:18:43,594 --> 02:18:44,927
So I'm gonna switch gears.

1558
02:18:46,010 --> 02:18:47,135
Don't look at him.

1559
02:18:47,219 --> 02:18:49,177
He's not the one
who's gonna have your wife

1560
02:18:49,260 --> 02:18:52,635
scraping your purple goopy brains
out of her carpet.

1561
02:18:52,719 --> 02:18:56,885
Unless you call off the airstrike now.

1562
02:18:56,969 --> 02:19:00,510
And if you're afraid
of going against Gravik,

1563
02:19:01,552 --> 02:19:02,594
I can protect you.

1564
02:19:03,094 --> 02:19:05,885
You couldn't protect yourself
coming through that door.

1565
02:19:06,385 --> 02:19:08,885
You're a shell
of the general you used to be.

1566
02:19:10,552 --> 02:19:11,927
Just wait outside?

1567
02:19:12,302 --> 02:19:14,677
Why don't you shapeshift back
into this piece of trash

1568
02:19:14,760 --> 02:19:16,927
and call in an abort
on that missile strike?

1569
02:19:17,010 --> 02:19:19,094
Great idea. Why didn't I think of that?

1570
02:19:19,510 --> 02:19:23,635
Maybe 'cause he's the only one
who knows the code word.

1571
02:19:23,719 --> 02:19:25,177
You got a code for us, Commodore?

1572
02:19:25,302 --> 02:19:28,052
ROBERT: You created this vacuum.
All Gravik did is fill it.

1573
02:19:28,344 --> 02:19:29,719
I want to talk to Cent Com.

1574
02:19:30,302 --> 02:19:32,302
These are Cent Com's orders.

1575
02:19:32,760 --> 02:19:35,469
Either you obey or you'll be removed.

1576
02:19:35,552 --> 02:19:36,760
Do you understand?

1577
02:19:38,010 --> 02:19:39,594
ROBERT: You could've led together.

1578
02:19:39,677 --> 02:19:43,760
Gravik offered you a partnership.
We would have stood by you proudly.

1579
02:19:43,844 --> 02:19:45,719
So stand with me now.

1580
02:19:45,802 --> 02:19:46,802
You're too late.

1581
02:19:46,927 --> 02:19:49,135
- Enough of this bull!
- (SCREAMS)

1582
02:19:49,677 --> 02:19:51,344
I'm giving you three seconds

1583
02:19:51,427 --> 02:19:53,677
to give me that code,
or I'm gonna aim higher,

1584
02:19:53,760 --> 02:19:55,219
or maybe lower.

1585
02:19:55,302 --> 02:19:56,302
- Give me the gun.
- One!

1586
02:19:56,427 --> 02:19:57,760
- Give me the...
- Two!

1587
02:19:57,844 --> 02:19:59,052
I said give me that gun!

1588
02:19:59,135 --> 02:20:03,094
You got minutes to figure out that code
if we can't make your friend here tell us.

1589
02:20:20,219 --> 02:20:21,219
Prepare to launch.

1590
02:20:23,177 --> 02:20:25,219
FURY: Getting close
to showtime here, Talos.

1591
02:20:26,177 --> 02:20:27,777
ROBERT: Traitors like you are the reason

1592
02:20:27,802 --> 02:20:31,052
people have been walking in exile
for 30 years.

1593
02:20:31,385 --> 02:20:33,302
- You sicken me.
- Shut up!

1594
02:20:33,385 --> 02:20:34,969
What's it gonna be, man?

1595
02:20:36,344 --> 02:20:38,760
You can't even keep
your daughter's loyalty.

1596
02:20:40,135 --> 02:20:43,260
Or is she the spineless traitor
feeding you information?

1597
02:20:45,844 --> 02:20:46,969
(GASPS)

1598
02:20:55,052 --> 02:20:56,719
(BEEPING)

1599
02:21:13,760 --> 02:21:14,760
G'IAH: <i>What is it?</i>

1600
02:21:15,010 --> 02:21:16,594
Commodore Robert Fairbanks.

1601
02:21:16,677 --> 02:21:19,885
<i>I need his
launch termination password now.</i>

1602
02:21:28,552 --> 02:21:30,552
(COMPUTER BEEPING)

1603
02:21:35,885 --> 02:21:39,094
- Good evening, friends.
- Operative G'iah. What can we do for you?

1604
02:21:41,760 --> 02:21:43,510
AUTOMATED VOICE: <i>Initiate go position.</i>

1605
02:21:52,719 --> 02:21:53,885
(COMPUTER BEEPS)

1606
02:22:06,469 --> 02:22:09,510
(VOICES CHATTERING INDISTINCTLY)

1607
02:22:20,219 --> 02:22:21,927
(YELLING INDISTINCTLY)

1608
02:22:25,177 --> 02:22:26,594
(CELL PHONE RINGS)

1609
02:22:28,594 --> 02:22:29,802
You got it?

1610
02:22:31,552 --> 02:22:33,094
Okay. Now run.

1611
02:22:41,135 --> 02:22:42,635
Initiating go position.

1612
02:22:47,802 --> 02:22:49,177
Initiating go position.

1613
02:22:49,844 --> 02:22:51,719
AUTOMATED VOICE: <i>Launch sequence underway.</i>

1614
02:22:54,885 --> 02:22:56,245
(MIMICS ROBERT) This is Fairbanks.

1615
02:22:58,219 --> 02:23:00,677
Abort exercise.

1616
02:23:01,719 --> 02:23:04,219
Code word, Zachary.

1617
02:23:06,052 --> 02:23:07,427
AUTOMATED VOICE: <i>Abort launch.</i>

1618
02:23:08,344 --> 02:23:09,719
<i>Abort launch.</i>

1619
02:23:09,844 --> 02:23:11,385
(ALARM BLARING)

1620
02:23:13,969 --> 02:23:15,219
(COMPUTER BEEPING)

1621
02:23:35,844 --> 02:23:38,635
- FURY: So, why didn't you take the deal?
- What deal?

1622
02:23:39,260 --> 02:23:40,344
Gravik's.

1623
02:23:40,469 --> 02:23:42,427
Gotta be hard for you
to be fighting with him

1624
02:23:42,510 --> 02:23:45,594
when deep down in your bones
you believe in what he's doing.

1625
02:23:46,344 --> 02:23:49,552
Shit. Thirty years,
you still don't know me better than that?

1626
02:23:49,969 --> 02:23:50,969
(SCOFFS)

1627
02:23:53,469 --> 02:23:56,052
All right, so make me understand.

1628
02:23:58,260 --> 02:24:00,885
I'm not with Gravik 'cause I'm with you.

1629
02:24:16,760 --> 02:24:18,302
(ENGINE REVS)

1630
02:24:27,885 --> 02:24:28,969
(G'IAH GROANS)

1631
02:24:38,885 --> 02:24:40,594
GRAVIK: Where are you off to, G'iah?

1632
02:24:41,635 --> 02:24:43,094
I heard about the failed strike.

1633
02:24:43,802 --> 02:24:45,219
Our men need exfiltration.

1634
02:24:46,135 --> 02:24:47,177
I didn't fail.

1635
02:24:48,594 --> 02:24:50,219
That plane would have been valuable.

1636
02:24:50,802 --> 02:24:53,510
Finding the traitor was essential.

1637
02:24:57,094 --> 02:24:58,427
Go on, turn around.

1638
02:24:59,719 --> 02:25:00,719
No.

1639
02:25:02,594 --> 02:25:03,844
You will look at me.

1640
02:25:04,802 --> 02:25:06,177
And you'll ask yourself,

1641
02:25:08,135 --> 02:25:09,885
are you a leader of Skrulls

1642
02:25:10,885 --> 02:25:11,885
or our worst enemy?

1643
02:25:12,010 --> 02:25:13,427
- (GUN FIRES)
- (GROANS)

1644
02:25:44,052 --> 02:25:45,635
(CELL PHONE VIBRATING)

1645
02:26:11,010 --> 02:26:14,760
WOMAN OVER PA:
<i>Platform 17 for the 16:42 to Teddington,</i>

1646
02:26:14,844 --> 02:26:18,344
<i>calling at Vauxhall, Clapham Junction,
Earlsfield, Wimbledon.</i>

1647
02:26:20,094 --> 02:26:21,885
(MAN SHOUTS)
<i>The National!</i>

1648
02:26:45,802 --> 02:26:47,969
- I'll give you some time alone.
- Hmm.

1649
02:26:52,469 --> 02:26:53,469
(DOOR CLOSES)

1650
02:27:13,260 --> 02:27:14,760
(CELL PHONE VIBRATING)

1651
02:27:19,385 --> 02:27:21,219
MAN ON PHONE: <i>St. James Church, one hour.</i>

1652
02:27:22,052 --> 02:27:23,635
I need to speak to Gravik.

1653
02:27:23,719 --> 02:27:25,177
<i>Yeah, well, you're talking to me.</i>

1654
02:27:26,177 --> 02:27:31,177
<font color="#ff8040">{\an8}Downloaded From MoviesMod.org</font>

1655
02:30:10,261 --> 02:30:17,824
<font color="#00ff00">{\an8}Downloaded From MoviesMod.org</font>

1656
02:30:18,824 --> 02:30:22,116
PRISCILLA: <i>Do I dare ask what
calamity must have transpired</i>

1657
02:30:22,199 --> 02:30:24,283
to bring you home to me?

1658
02:30:26,574 --> 02:30:28,199
(CROWD SCREAMING)

1659
02:30:28,324 --> 02:30:31,366
How do you explain
Mr. Fury's presence in Moscow?

1660
02:30:31,533 --> 02:30:34,116
They sent you to fire me?

1661
02:30:34,658 --> 02:30:35,699
I volunteered.

1662
02:30:35,783 --> 02:30:38,408
That mess that you created in Moscow
that resulted in getting

1663
02:30:38,491 --> 02:30:40,783
<i>- one of our best people murdered?</i>
- (GUN FIRES)

1664
02:30:40,866 --> 02:30:42,824
You earned all this smoke, brother.

1665
02:30:43,491 --> 02:30:44,731
GRAVIK: <i>At the Council meeting,</i>

1666
02:30:44,783 --> 02:30:47,866
I told you I had a plan
for taking Earth as our own.

1667
02:30:49,283 --> 02:30:51,324
<i>The heroes of Earth will react.</i>

1668
02:30:51,949 --> 02:30:56,699
<i>The only way we can counter that
is to become super ourselves.</i>

1669
02:30:57,408 --> 02:30:58,408
<i>All of us.</i>

1670
02:30:59,033 --> 02:31:00,241
Super Skrulls.

1671
02:31:00,408 --> 02:31:01,408
TALOS: <i>G'iah.</i>

1672
02:31:01,574 --> 02:31:02,616
Run.

1673
02:31:05,324 --> 02:31:06,449
(GROANS)

1674
02:31:07,658 --> 02:31:09,533
- Go on, turn around.
- G'IAH: No.

1675
02:31:09,991 --> 02:31:11,699
Are you a leader of Skrulls

1676
02:31:12,616 --> 02:31:13,741
or our worst enemy?

1677
02:31:13,908 --> 02:31:15,033
- (GUN FIRES)
- (GROANS)

1678
02:31:21,949 --> 02:31:23,709
MAN ON THE PHONE: <i>St. James Church,
one hour.</i>

1679
02:32:18,658 --> 02:32:19,866
(GASPS)

1680
02:34:48,116 --> 02:34:50,116
(PEOPLE CHATTERING INDISTINCTLY)

1681
02:35:15,283 --> 02:35:19,199
As I was watching all the news coverage
of those guys'

1682
02:35:19,283 --> 02:35:22,408
heroics over in the States,
strangest thing,

1683
02:35:22,658 --> 02:35:24,616
I kept having this feeling

1684
02:35:24,699 --> 02:35:28,491
that someone I know had something to do
with getting them all together.

1685
02:35:31,283 --> 02:35:34,491
And what if it was someone you know?

1686
02:35:35,491 --> 02:35:36,699
Wouldn't surprise me.

1687
02:35:37,491 --> 02:35:38,533
Why is that?

1688
02:35:39,241 --> 02:35:44,116
Because if he's the man I think he is,
he has a powerful sense of righteousness.

1689
02:35:45,908 --> 02:35:50,574
He understands that the universe
is a dangerous place.

1690
02:35:51,866 --> 02:35:54,741
That home is worth fighting for.

1691
02:35:55,616 --> 02:35:57,658
And that the weak are worth protecting.

1692
02:36:02,991 --> 02:36:03,991
Good book?

1693
02:36:05,283 --> 02:36:06,699
It's a collection of poems.

1694
02:36:08,199 --> 02:36:09,449
Raymond Carver.

1695
02:36:10,741 --> 02:36:13,866
- You familiar?
- Nah. More of a history guy myself.

1696
02:36:14,366 --> 02:36:16,158
He's known for his brevity.

1697
02:36:16,449 --> 02:36:19,866
I mean, some of his poems
are just three or four lines,

1698
02:36:20,408 --> 02:36:22,866
but they pack a punch.

1699
02:36:23,283 --> 02:36:24,408
Do you have a favorite?

1700
02:36:25,658 --> 02:36:27,116
It's called <i>Late Fragment.</i>

1701
02:36:27,283 --> 02:36:28,491
Hmm. How's it go?

1702
02:36:30,949 --> 02:36:32,033
Uh...

1703
02:36:32,616 --> 02:36:37,241
Actually, it's a conversation
between two people.

1704
02:36:39,366 --> 02:36:40,824
You read the first line.

1705
02:36:45,116 --> 02:36:49,283
"And did you get
what you wanted from this life,

1706
02:36:49,908 --> 02:36:51,116
"even so?"

1707
02:36:53,866 --> 02:36:54,866
"I did."

1708
02:36:56,491 --> 02:36:57,949
"And what did you want?"

1709
02:37:00,241 --> 02:37:02,741
"To call myself beloved,

1710
02:37:03,908 --> 02:37:07,699
"to feel myself beloved on the earth."

1711
02:37:21,074 --> 02:37:23,074
(CHOIR SINGING HYMN)

1712
02:37:55,741 --> 02:37:56,741
(RHODEY SIGHS)

1713
02:38:05,366 --> 02:38:08,574
- Fury was fired a couple of days ago.
- Fired?

1714
02:38:09,866 --> 02:38:10,866
How'd that happen?

1715
02:38:11,199 --> 02:38:13,699
President Ritson must have found out
he was in Moscow.

1716
02:38:13,783 --> 02:38:17,033
(CHUCKLES) President Ritson
doesn't find out that the sun's come up

1717
02:38:17,199 --> 02:38:18,199
unless I brief him.

1718
02:38:18,283 --> 02:38:20,574
I fired Fury, okay?

1719
02:38:20,658 --> 02:38:23,783
No, I'm sorry, correction,
I DDT'd that dude from the top rope.

1720
02:38:24,449 --> 02:38:27,616
Yeah, it was like Undertaker level.
It was really impressive.

1721
02:38:28,283 --> 02:38:30,824
I don't understand. If it was you...

1722
